{"modelInput":{"anthropic_version":"bedrock-2023-05-31","max_tokens":1024,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Extract the following details from the job description:\n\nEmployment Details:\n- Type of employment (FULL_TIME, PART_TIME, INTERNSHIP, CONTRACT, etc.)\n- Department (e.g., hr, marketing, sales, tech)\n- Company name\n- Salary range (minimum and maximum values)\n- Years of experience required (numeric values for min and max)\n- Notice period requirements (in months)\n\nSkills Requirements:\n- Core skills required for the role\n- Technical skills required (programming languages, software, etc.)\n- Soft skills and interpersonal abilities\n- Miscellaneous skills that don't fit other categories\n\nImportant Instructions:\n- Extract ONLY information explicitly mentioned in the job description\n- Do not infer or fabricate any details not present in the text\n- For type of employment, use UPPERCASE (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n- For department, use lowercase (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n- For company name, use UPPERCASE\n- For all skills, use lowercase format\n- If information for any field is not available, return an empty array or null as appropriate\n- If typeofEmployment or companyName are already present, do not update them\n\nHere is the job description:\n\nCOMPANY DESCRIPTION\n\nWork with Us. Change the World.\n\nAt AECOM, we're delivering a better world. Whether improving your commute,\nkeeping the lights on, providing access to clean water, or transforming\nskylines, our work helps people and communities thrive. We are the world's\ntrusted infrastructure consulting firm, partnering with clients to solve the\nworld’s most complex challenges and build legacies for future generations.\n\nThere has never been a better time to be at AECOM. With accelerating\ninfrastructure investment worldwide, our services are in great demand. We invite\nyou to bring your bold ideas and big dreams and become part of a global team of\nover 50,000 planners, designers, engineers, scientists, digital innovators,\nprogram and construction managers and other professionals delivering projects\nthat create a positive and tangible impact around the world.\n\nWe're one global team driven by our common purpose to deliver a better world.\nJoin us.\n\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION\n\nResponsible for engineering, design, and modification activities related to\nmechanical equipment, vessels and tanks and piping systems including equipment\nand piping specifications and procurement. May be involved with the support of\ninstallation and operation & maintenance of equipment.\n\nDiscipline concerning air conditioning, refrigeration, ventilation, combustion,\nheat transfer, energy, power, fuels, propulsion, machinery, tools,\nmanufacturing, fluids, plumbing, fire suppression systems and devices, water\nsupplies and pumping systems for fire protection.\n\nDiscipline covers the ability to solve problems that deliver and optimise safe,\nsustainable and ethical solutions for the design, production and operation of\ndevices, machines, structures, processes and systems involving mechanical\nelements.\n\nDuties and Responsibilities\n\n * Serve as senior technical resource and technical advisor for the team\n * Provide specialised technical input to studies and design for staff's\n   specific area of expertise\n * Develop study and design procedures to facilitate high quality cost effective\n   work by others\n * Participate in interdisciplinary review of project deliverables\n * Develop construction cost estimates and estimates of technical efforts for\n   projects\n * Use expertise in all steps of completing discipline component of PS&E package\n * Perform quality control review of design calculations or drawings\n * Prepare technical specification sections\n * Provide input to the development of engineering budget and schedule to meet\n   requirements\n * Lead the design of HVAC systems for healthcare facilities, ensuring\n   compliance with relevant healthcare standards and regulations\n * Develop and implement innovative solutions for infection control and air\n   quality management in medical environments\n * Mentor and guide junior engineers, fostering their professional development\n   and technical expertise\n * Collaborate with cross-functional teams to integrate HVAC designs with other\n   building systems\n * Conduct energy modelling and analysis to optimise system performance and\n   reduce environmental impact\n * Liaise with clients, architects, and contractors to ensure project\n   requirements are met and designs are effectively implemented\n * Oversee the commissioning process for HVAC systems in healthcare projects\n * Stay abreast of emerging technologies and best practices in HVAC design for\n   healthcare applications\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\n * BE in Mechanical Engineering.\n * 10+ years of experience working in Mechanical Engineering design, with a\n   focus on HVAC systems for healthcare facilities.\n * Experience in the UK & UAE Building projects, particularly in the healthcare\n   sector.\n * Proven track record in the design of Health Care, residential, commercial,\n   retail and hospitality sectors.\n * Advanced knowledge of software applications including IES, HAP, Trace, Elite,\n   MEP Revit, Excel, PowerPoint, and Word.\n * Demonstrated ability to lead and mentor junior engineers in HVAC design and\n   engineering principles.\n * In-depth understanding of healthcare-specific HVAC requirements, including\n   infection control and air quality management.\n * Familiarity with relevant healthcare standards and regulations in the UK and\n   UAE, such as HTM 03-01 and ASHRAE Standard 170.\n * Experience in energy modelling and analysis for optimising HVAC system\n   performance in healthcare settings.\n * Strong project management skills with the ability to oversee multiple\n   projects simultaneously.\n * Excellent communication skills for liaising with clients, architects, and\n   contractors.\n * Professional registration as a Chartered Engineer (CEng) with the Engineering\n   Council UK or equivalent professional body.\n * LEED or BREEAM accreditation is highly desirable.\n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\nAbout AECOM \n\nAECOM is proud to offer comprehensive benefits to meet the diverse needs of our\nemployees. Depending on your employment status, AECOM benefits may include\nmedical, dental, vision, life, AD&D, disability benefits, paid time off, leaves\nof absences, voluntary benefits, perks, flexible work options, well-being\nresources, employee assistance program, business travel insurance, service\nrecognition awards, retirement savings plan, and employee stock purchase plan. \n\nAECOM is the global infrastructure leader, committed to delivering a better\nworld. As a trusted professional services firm powered by deep technical\nabilities, we solve our clients’ complex challenges in water, environment,\nenergy, transportation and buildings. Our teams partner with public- and\nprivate-sector clients to create innovative, sustainable and resilient solutions\nthroughout the project lifecycle – from advisory, planning, design and\nengineering to program and construction management. AECOM is a Fortune 500 firm\nthat had revenue of $16.1 billion in fiscal year 2024. Learn more at aecom.com. \n\nWhat makes AECOM a great place to work \n\nYou will be part of a global team that champions your growth and career\nambitions. Work on groundbreaking projects - both in your local community and on\na global scale - that are transforming our industry and shaping the future. With\ncutting-edge technology and a network of experts, you’ll have the resources to\nmake a real impact. Our award-winning training and development programs are\ndesigned to expand your technical expertise and leadership skills, helping you\nbuild the career you’ve always envisioned. Here, you’ll find a welcoming\nworkplace built on respect, collaboration and community - where you have the\nfreedom to grow in a world of opportunity. \n\nAs an Equal Opportunity Employer, we believe in your potential and are here to\nhelp you achieve it. All your information will be kept confidential according to\nEEO guidelines. \n\nReturn only the following JSON structure with extracted values. Do not provide any additional content, explanations, or details:\n\n{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n  \"department\": \"string\", // lowercase format (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n  \"companyName\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": number // in months, if mentioned\n}"}]}]},"modelOutput":{"id":"msg_bdrk_01Fy4WeicTceUbiKnz3MGpS7","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"FULL_TIME\",\n  \"department\": \"engineering\",\n  \"companyName\": \"AECOM\",\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": null,\n    \"max\": null\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": 10,\n    \"max\": null\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"mechanical engineering\",\n    \"hvac systems design\",\n    \"healthcare facility design\",\n    \"construction cost estimation\",\n    \"technical specification writing\",\n    \"quality control\",\n    \"infection control\",\n    \"air quality management\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"ies\",\n    \"hap\",\n    \"trace\",\n    \"elite\",\n    \"mep revit\",\n    \"excel\",\n    \"powerpoint\",\n    \"word\",\n    \"energy modeling\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"leadership\",\n    \"mentoring\",\n    \"communication\",\n    \"project management\",\n    \"client liaison\",\n    \"team collaboration\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"uk & uae building regulations knowledge\",\n    \"htm 03-01 knowledge\",\n    \"ashrae standard 170 knowledge\",\n    \"chartered engineer certification\",\n    \"leed or breeam accreditation\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": null\n}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2002,"output_tokens":342}},"recordId":"01JVA02K4BMPWG9TE9SMYK7F7N"}
{"modelInput":{"anthropic_version":"bedrock-2023-05-31","max_tokens":1024,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Extract the following details from the job description:\n\nEmployment Details:\n- Type of employment (FULL_TIME, PART_TIME, INTERNSHIP, CONTRACT, etc.)\n- Department (e.g., hr, marketing, sales, tech)\n- Company name\n- Salary range (minimum and maximum values)\n- Years of experience required (numeric values for min and max)\n- Notice period requirements (in months)\n\nSkills Requirements:\n- Core skills required for the role\n- Technical skills required (programming languages, software, etc.)\n- Soft skills and interpersonal abilities\n- Miscellaneous skills that don't fit other categories\n\nImportant Instructions:\n- Extract ONLY information explicitly mentioned in the job description\n- Do not infer or fabricate any details not present in the text\n- For type of employment, use UPPERCASE (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n- For department, use lowercase (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n- For company name, use UPPERCASE\n- For all skills, use lowercase format\n- If information for any field is not available, return an empty array or null as appropriate\n- If typeofEmployment or companyName are already present, do not update them\n\nHere is the job description:\n\nCOMPANY DESCRIPTION\n\nBosch Global Software Technologies Private Limited is a 100% owned subsidiary of\nRobert Bosch GmbH, one of the world's leading global supplier of technology and\nservices, offering end-to-end Engineering, IT and Business Solutions. With over\n28,200+ associates, it’s the largest software development center of Bosch,\noutside Germany, indicating that it is the Technology Powerhouse of Bosch in\nIndia with a global footprint and presence in the US, Europe and the Asia\nPacific region.\n\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION\n\nRoles & Responsibilities :\n\nExperience in Model based development (MBD), Plant modeling, m- scripting and\nauto code generation using Matlab/Simulink.\n\n * Autocode generation tools Simulink Coder/ Embedded coder/TargetLink\n\n * Good exposure to System modelling, Control theory and Embedded Software\n   architecture\n\n * Ability to understand requirements and translate them into suitable solution\n   architecture.\n\n * Experience in MIL-SIL testing using Mathwork Tools such as MATLAB/Simulink,\n   Stateflow, SimulinkTest manager.\n\n * Experience in testing of ECU Control Software in SIL (Software-in-Loop) \n\n * Integrate plant model with multiple virtual ECUs to perform real time testing\n   of controllers using Software-In-the-Loop setups.\n\n * Experience working in any of the engineering domains like ADAS, EV, BCM,\n   Charging & Energy storage systems\n\n * Basic know how in software build and embedded C / C ++/python. \n   \n   * Automotive/embedded industry background will be an added advantage.\n\nReturn only the following JSON structure with extracted values. Do not provide any additional content, explanations, or details:\n\n{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n  \"department\": \"string\", // lowercase format (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n  \"companyName\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": number // in months, if mentioned\n}"}]}]},"modelOutput":{"id":"msg_bdrk_015AiW4rWWc8Lid21hkAjK41","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": null,\n  \"department\": \"tech\",\n  \"companyName\": \"BOSCH GLOBAL SOFTWARE TECHNOLOGIES PRIVATE LIMITED\",\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": null,\n    \"max\": null\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": null,\n    \"max\": null\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"model based development\",\n    \"plant modeling\",\n    \"control theory\",\n    \"embedded software architecture\",\n    \"system modelling\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"matlab\",\n    \"simulink\",\n    \"m-scripting\",\n    \"simulink coder\",\n    \"embedded coder\",\n    \"targetlink\",\n    \"stateflow\",\n    \"simulinktest manager\",\n    \"c++\",\n    \"c\",\n    \"python\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"requirement analysis\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"adas\",\n    \"ev\",\n    \"bcm\",\n    \"charging systems\",\n    \"energy storage systems\",\n    \"automotive domain\",\n    \"embedded systems\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": null\n}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":927,"output_tokens":303}},"recordId":"01JVA02K4EV3V36KS6X2QZWA55"}
{"modelInput":{"anthropic_version":"bedrock-2023-05-31","max_tokens":1024,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Extract the following details from the job description:\n\nEmployment Details:\n- Type of employment (FULL_TIME, PART_TIME, INTERNSHIP, CONTRACT, etc.)\n- Department (e.g., hr, marketing, sales, tech)\n- Company name\n- Salary range (minimum and maximum values)\n- Years of experience required (numeric values for min and max)\n- Notice period requirements (in months)\n\nSkills Requirements:\n- Core skills required for the role\n- Technical skills required (programming languages, software, etc.)\n- Soft skills and interpersonal abilities\n- Miscellaneous skills that don't fit other categories\n\nImportant Instructions:\n- Extract ONLY information explicitly mentioned in the job description\n- Do not infer or fabricate any details not present in the text\n- For type of employment, use UPPERCASE (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n- For department, use lowercase (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n- For company name, use UPPERCASE\n- For all skills, use lowercase format\n- If information for any field is not available, return an empty array or null as appropriate\n- If typeofEmployment or companyName are already present, do not update them\n\nHere is the job description:\n\nCOMPANY DESCRIPTION\n\nWork with Us. Change the World.\n\nAt AECOM, we're delivering a better world. Whether improving your commute,\nkeeping the lights on, providing access to clean water, or transforming\nskylines, our work helps people and communities thrive. We are the world's\ntrusted infrastructure consulting firm, partnering with clients to solve the\nworld’s most complex challenges and build legacies for future generations.\n\nThere has never been a better time to be at AECOM. With accelerating\ninfrastructure investment worldwide, our services are in great demand. We invite\nyou to bring your bold ideas and big dreams and become part of a global team of\nover 50,000 planners, designers, engineers, scientists, digital innovators,\nprogram and construction managers and other professionals delivering projects\nthat create a positive and tangible impact around the world.\n\nWe're one global team driven by our common purpose to deliver a better world.\nJoin us.\n\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION\n\nDuties and Responsibilities\n\n• Performs specific and moderate portions of a broader assignment of an\nexperienced engineer.\n\n * Gathers and correlates basic engineering data using established and\n   well-defined procedures.\n * Works on detailed or routine engineering assignments involving calculations\n   and relatively simple tests.\n * Proposes approach to solve new problems encountered using modifications of\n   standard procedures or methods developed in previous assignments.\n * Identifies discrepancies in results.\n * Provides guidance to entry level engineers.\n * Performs work in accordance with agreed upon budget and schedule with little\n   supervision.\n * Independently performs all the tasks necessary to complete primary design\n   elements for engineering works.\n * Performance at this level requires developmental experience in a professional\n   position.\n * Develops and reviews HVAC system designs, including load calculations,\n   equipment selection, and ductwork layouts.\n * Collaborates with architects, structural engineers, and other disciplines to\n   ensure integrated building systems.\n * Conducts energy modeling and analysis to optimize HVAC system performance and\n   efficiency.\n * Prepares technical specifications, reports, and construction documents for\n   HVAC projects.\n * Participates in client meetings and site visits to assess project\n   requirements and troubleshoot issues.\n   \n    \n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\nMinimum Requirements\n\nEnergy Modeling, Building Performance analysis & IES Software skills listed in\ndetail below.\n\n \n\n 1.  Utilize energy modeling software like IES VE to simulate building\n     performance and energy consumption\n 2.  Analyze data received from client and energy results to provide the best\n     energy-efficient solutions to team\n 3.  Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams for various inputs and outputs to\n     do the efficient design process\n 4.  Ability to work on Cooling/Heating loads, Energy consumption and building\n     performance in IES VE or any other modeling software\n 5.  Familiarity with ASHRAE 90.1, 62.1, 55 and CIBSE requirements\n 6.  Knowledge of Mechanical system architecture and components\n 7.  Bachelor's degree in Mechanical Engineering or related field; Master's\n     degree preferred\n 8.  Professional Engineering (PE) license in HVAC or Mechanical Engineering\n 9.  Minimum of 8 years of experience in HVAC system design for commercial and\n     industrial buildings\n 10. Proficiency in AutoCAD, Revit MEP, and other relevant design software\n 11. Strong understanding of building codes and regulations related to HVAC\n     systems\n 12. Experience with sustainable design practices and LEED certification process\n 13. Excellent project management and communication skills\n 14. Ability to mentor junior engineers and lead design teams\n 15. Demonstrated problem-solving skills and attention to detail\n     \n      \n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\nAbout AECOM \n\nAECOM is proud to offer comprehensive benefits to meet the diverse needs of our\nemployees. Depending on your employment status, AECOM benefits may include\nmedical, dental, vision, life, AD&D, disability benefits, paid time off, leaves\nof absences, voluntary benefits, perks, flexible work options, well-being\nresources, employee assistance program, business travel insurance, service\nrecognition awards, retirement savings plan, and employee stock purchase plan. \n\nAECOM is the global infrastructure leader, committed to delivering a better\nworld. As a trusted professional services firm powered by deep technical\nabilities, we solve our clients’ complex challenges in water, environment,\nenergy, transportation and buildings. Our teams partner with public- and\nprivate-sector clients to create innovative, sustainable and resilient solutions\nthroughout the project lifecycle – from advisory, planning, design and\nengineering to program and construction management. AECOM is a Fortune 500 firm\nthat had revenue of $16.1 billion in fiscal year 2024. Learn more at aecom.com. \n\nWhat makes AECOM a great place to work \n\nYou will be part of a global team that champions your growth and career\nambitions. Work on groundbreaking projects - both in your local community and on\na global scale - that are transforming our industry and shaping the future. With\ncutting-edge technology and a network of experts, you’ll have the resources to\nmake a real impact. Our award-winning training and development programs are\ndesigned to expand your technical expertise and leadership skills, helping you\nbuild the career you’ve always envisioned. Here, you’ll find a welcoming\nworkplace built on respect, collaboration and community - where you have the\nfreedom to grow in a world of opportunity. \n\nAs an Equal Opportunity Employer, we believe in your potential and are here to\nhelp you achieve it. All your information will be kept confidential according to\nEEO guidelines. \n\nReturn only the following JSON structure with extracted values. Do not provide any additional content, explanations, or details:\n\n{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n  \"department\": \"string\", // lowercase format (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n  \"companyName\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": number // in months, if mentioned\n}"}]}]},"modelOutput":{"id":"msg_bdrk_011P54ZBLDfFSNgfRj9Hr7n2","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"FULL_TIME\",\n  \"department\": \"engineering\",\n  \"companyName\": \"AECOM\",\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": null,\n    \"max\": null\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": 8,\n    \"max\": null\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"hvac system design\",\n    \"mechanical engineering\",\n    \"building performance analysis\",\n    \"energy modeling\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"ies ve\",\n    \"autocad\",\n    \"revit mep\",\n    \"energy modeling software\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"communication\",\n    \"mentoring\",\n    \"problem-solving\",\n    \"attention to detail\",\n    \"collaboration\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"ashrae standards knowledge\",\n    \"building codes knowledge\",\n    \"leed certification process\",\n    \"sustainable design practices\",\n    \"project management\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": null\n}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1844,"output_tokens":270}},"recordId":"01JVA02K4FG7XQ9T6DH4WB8XJW"}
{"modelInput":{"anthropic_version":"bedrock-2023-05-31","max_tokens":1024,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Extract the following details from the job description:\n\nEmployment Details:\n- Type of employment (FULL_TIME, PART_TIME, INTERNSHIP, CONTRACT, etc.)\n- Department (e.g., hr, marketing, sales, tech)\n- Company name\n- Salary range (minimum and maximum values)\n- Years of experience required (numeric values for min and max)\n- Notice period requirements (in months)\n\nSkills Requirements:\n- Core skills required for the role\n- Technical skills required (programming languages, software, etc.)\n- Soft skills and interpersonal abilities\n- Miscellaneous skills that don't fit other categories\n\nImportant Instructions:\n- Extract ONLY information explicitly mentioned in the job description\n- Do not infer or fabricate any details not present in the text\n- For type of employment, use UPPERCASE (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n- For department, use lowercase (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n- For company name, use UPPERCASE\n- For all skills, use lowercase format\n- If information for any field is not available, return an empty array or null as appropriate\n- If typeofEmployment or companyName are already present, do not update them\n\nHere is the job description:\n\nCOMPANY DESCRIPTION\n\nVisa is a world leader in payments and technology, with over 259 billion\npayments transactions flowing safely between consumers, merchants, financial\ninstitutions, and government entities in more than 200 countries and territories\neach year. Our mission is to connect the world through the most innovative,\nconvenient, reliable, and secure payments network, enabling individuals,\nbusinesses, and economies to thrive while driven by a common purpose – to uplift\neveryone, everywhere by being the best way to pay and be paid.\n\nMake an impact with a purpose-driven industry leader. Join us today and\nexperience Life at Visa.\n\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION\n\nThe Risk and Identity Solutions (RaIS) is a key component of the Value-Added\nServices (VAS) PD within Visa. VAS-RaIS has a suite of high visibility,\nhigh-volume, revenue earning applications that provide solutions related to Risk\nManagement, Identity and Authentication. Our capabilities are used extensively\nby key players in the payment eco-space across the globe.\n\nThe Senior Project Analyst in the RaIS PMO performs the duties of a Technical\nProgram Manager. Our Technical Program Managers are highly visible leaders,\nbuilding bridges across Visa to ensure projects are effectively developed,\nintegrated and deployed with quality and on time delivery into our production\nsystems.\n\nAs a Technical Program Manager for our RaIS team, you will drive quality and\nvelocity of our technology.  You should be comfortable with owning issues and\nmanaging the outcome. You enjoy driving, resolving, facilitating and follow up.\nYou understand the risks and the trade-offs and are both technical and process\nfocused.\n\nA strong candidate will have a solid experience with technology/ product program\nmanagement, release management, x-functional team leadership, as well as superb\nskills in communications, business analysis, problem-solving, cross-team\ncoordination, communications, processes, and change management. The ideal\ncandidate is not just a facilitator or project plan tracker but ensures things\nget done. The ideal candidate must have a drive to get things done and a make it\nhappen attitude.\n\n \n\nEssential Functions\n\n * Key resource to lead/support end-to-end planning and execution of one or more\n   projects and/or Agile teams that are part of a larger program. Contribute to\n   and facilitate negotiations on scope, schedule, budget, risks, releases and\n   communications.\n * Coach multiple teams through the software development life cycle using Agile,\n   Scrum, and Lean practices and work cross-functionally throughout the company\n   to ensure projects are developed and deployed with quality and timely\n   delivery into our production systems. \n * Ask thoughtful questions to help our customers, product owners, and product\n   managers to maximize ROI and meet company objectives. Understand product\n   strategy and benefits of key deliverables in area of responsibility.\n * Work with product owner to promote and contribute to the improvement of the\n   product backlog\n * Facilitate discussion and conflict resolution\n * Coach team in estimation techniques\n * Lead Agile release planning\n * Ensure clear communication and collaboration among the Product Owner and\n   members of the Development team   \n * Ensure the program and projects are in compliance with Visa's Project\n   Management Methodology and Key Controls and that accurate and timely\n   information is reported regularly on program progress and financial status.\n * Provide timely and accurate reporting to all stakeholders. Hold regular cross\n   organizational management briefings.\n * Lead boldly and utilize hard and soft skills to influence participants of all\n   levels towards the common goal.\n * Proactively identify and mitigate risks and issues.\n * Identify and manage dependencies and impacts \n * Drive improvement in overall efficiency and reliability of our release and\n   deployment processes.\n * Exercise independent judgment with minimal direction from supervisor\n\nThis is a hybrid position. Expectation of days in office will be confirmed by\nyour Hiring Manager.\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\nBasic Qualifications\n• 8 or more years of relevant work experience with a Bachelor's Degree or with\nan advanced degree.\n• Excellent analytical skills and enthusiastic problem solver\n• Strong leadership qualities and organizational skills as well as the ability\nto adapt quickly to changing priorities, assignments, and roles.\n• Strong knowledge of Project Management and SDLC principles and practices and\nagile frameworks.\n• Excellent verbal, written, and presentation skills. A demonstrated ability to\neffectively document and communicate technical and business issues and solutions\nto appropriate organizational levels.\n• Ability to work with minimal guidance. Ability to prioritize work, multi-task\nand manage one’s time.\n• Ability to thoroughly understand complex business and technical issues and\ninfluence decision making at all levels of the organization without formal\nreporting structure authority\n\n• Good to have SPC certification or SAFe methodology implementation experience.\n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\nVisa is an EEO Employer. Qualified applicants will receive consideration for\nemployment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, sexual\norientation, gender identity, disability or protected veteran status. Visa will\nalso consider for employment qualified applicants with criminal histories in a\nmanner consistent with EEOC guidelines and applicable local law.\n\nReturn only the following JSON structure with extracted values. Do not provide any additional content, explanations, or details:\n\n{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n  \"department\": \"string\", // lowercase format (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n  \"companyName\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": number // in months, if mentioned\n}"}]}]},"modelOutput":{"id":"msg_bdrk_01MnqpyaTQh9sQnJJCjn5wmr","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"FULL_TIME\",\n  \"department\": \"tech\",\n  \"companyName\": \"VISA\",\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": null,\n    \"max\": null\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": 8,\n    \"max\": null\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"project management\",\n    \"sdlc\",\n    \"agile frameworks\",\n    \"release management\",\n    \"safe methodology\",\n    \"scrum\",\n    \"lean practices\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"leadership\",\n    \"communication\",\n    \"analytical thinking\",\n    \"problem solving\",\n    \"organizational skills\",\n    \"conflict resolution\",\n    \"stakeholder management\",\n    \"adaptability\",\n    \"time management\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"risk management\",\n    \"cross-team coordination\",\n    \"estimation techniques\",\n    \"change management\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": null\n}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1695,"output_tokens":267}},"recordId":"01JVA02K4GG34D6B6GCA6F370V"}
{"modelInput":{"anthropic_version":"bedrock-2023-05-31","max_tokens":1024,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Extract the following details from the job description:\n\nEmployment Details:\n- Type of employment (FULL_TIME, PART_TIME, INTERNSHIP, CONTRACT, etc.)\n- Department (e.g., hr, marketing, sales, tech)\n- Company name\n- Salary range (minimum and maximum values)\n- Years of experience required (numeric values for min and max)\n- Notice period requirements (in months)\n\nSkills Requirements:\n- Core skills required for the role\n- Technical skills required (programming languages, software, etc.)\n- Soft skills and interpersonal abilities\n- Miscellaneous skills that don't fit other categories\n\nImportant Instructions:\n- Extract ONLY information explicitly mentioned in the job description\n- Do not infer or fabricate any details not present in the text\n- For type of employment, use UPPERCASE (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n- For department, use lowercase (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n- For company name, use UPPERCASE\n- For all skills, use lowercase format\n- If information for any field is not available, return an empty array or null as appropriate\n- If typeofEmployment or companyName are already present, do not update them\n\nHere is the job description:\n\nJob Title: Chief Marketing Strategist & Creative Lead\n\n\n\nLocation: [Hyderabad – In-House, Full-Time]\n\n\n\nType: Full-Time, On-Site\n\n\n\nSalary Range: ₹2.0L – ₹3.5L/month (Based on experience + performance incentives)\n\n\n\n⸻\n\n\n\n🧠 Role Overview:\n\n\n\nWe are seeking a visionary yet hands-on marketing leader who will own our brand\nand marketing\n\n\n\nend-to-end across our three key verticals: Jewelry, Gemstones, and Charitable\nOrganization.\n\n\n\nThis role is for someone who has successfully led marketing functions, directed\ncreative teams,\n\n\n\nmanaged campaign outcomes, and is passionate about creating high-impact brand\nstories and\n\n\n\nmeasurable results.\n\n\n\nYou will collaborate with our in-house ad expert, videographer, editor, and\nphotographers — but\n\n\n\nthe ideation, direction, calendar planning, and creative quality will be your\nresponsibility.\n\n\n\n⸻\n\n\n\n🎯 Key Responsibilities:\n\n\n\n🔸 Strategy & Calendar Leadership:\n\n\n\n• Build marketing strategies for each brand objective (e.g., wedding jewelry\nsales,\n\n\n\ngemstone education, charity outreach).\n\n\n\n• Identify ideal marketing mediums (digital, print, influencer, PR, local\nevents) for\n\n\n\nevery campaign.\n\n\n\n• Design and own the marketing calendar and coordinate execution timelines\nacross\n\n\n\nplatforms.\n\n\n\n🔸 Creative Leadership:\n\n\n\n• Ideate and brief content – including photoshoots, video scripts, brochure\nconcepts,\n\n\n\nreels, social ads.\n\n\n\n• Collaborate with creatives to deliver high-quality, on-brand assets.\n\n\n\n• Oversee editing, storytelling, post-production, and final approvals.\n\n\n\n• Ensure all content meets aesthetic, quality, and impact standards.\n\n\n\n🔸 Campaign Execution:\n\n\n\n• Translate ideas into actionable campaigns with clear KPIs.\n\n\n\n• Sync with the ad expert for implementation and reporting.\n\n\n\n• Review campaign performance and apply insights to future planning.\n\n\n\n🔸 Innovation & Resources:\n\n\n\n• Use AI tools (content generation, video scripts, visuals) to speed up\nideation.\n\n\n\n• Build or recommend a team when needed — freelance editors, writers, PR\n\n\n\nprofessionals, etc.\n\n\n\n• Be the “go-to” person for creative execution and strategic direction.🔸\nCommunication & Influence:\n\n\n\n• Engage influencers if required, plan collaborations and integrations.\n\n\n\n• Suggest and coordinate PR activities or media presence.\n\n\n\n• Represent the brand vision in all content — from Instagram to brochures.\n\n\n\n⸻\n\n\n\n✅ Required Experience & Skills:\n\n\n\n• Minimum 6–10 years in brand marketing / campaign leadership roles.\n\n\n\n• Proven experience in jewelry, fashion, luxury, or lifestyle industries\npreferred.\n\n\n\n• Strong aesthetic and storytelling sense.\n\n\n\n• Skilled in working with videographers, photographers, editors, designers.\n\n\n\n• Experience creating multi-format content (reels, print, 3D, motion graphics,\netc.)\n\n\n\n• Familiarity with tools like Canva, ChatGPT, Midjourney, Notion (or\nequivalents).\n\n\n\n• Basic knowledge of ad formats, consumer funnels, and marketing metrics.\n\n\n\n• Excellent communication and leadership skills.\n\n\n\n• Track record of owning a result and delivering it.\n\n\n\n⸻\n\n\n\n💰 Compensation (Indicative):\n\n\n\n• Base Salary: ₹2.0L – ₹3.5L/month (Depending on profile & region)\n\n\n\n• Performance Bonus: ₹0.5L–₹1L/month for measurable achievements (leads,\n\n\n\nfootfall, brand recall)\n\n\n\n• Annual Growth & Annual bonus available based on Results, Eﬃciency\n\n\n\n⸻\n\n\n\n🎯 Success in This Role Means:\n\n\n\n• Consistent campaign execution that improves brand visibility and lead quality\n\n\n\n• Creatives that are aesthetic, strategic, and high-performing\n\n\n\n• A content pipeline that runs like clockwork\n\n\n\n• A marketing plan that syncs with business goals and customer needs\n\n\n\n• Increase in foot fool of exact Target Audience\n\n\n\n• Active App user targets met\n\n\n\n⸻\n\nReturn only the following JSON structure with extracted values. Do not provide any additional content, explanations, or details:\n\n{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n  \"department\": \"string\", // lowercase format (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n  \"companyName\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": number // in months, if mentioned\n}"}]}]},"modelOutput":{"id":"msg_bdrk_01ULiGU45nSTXujDZkwMxzfz","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"FULL_TIME\",\n  \"department\": \"marketing\",\n  \"companyName\": null,\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": 200000,\n    \"max\": 350000\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": 6,\n    \"max\": 10\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"brand marketing\",\n    \"campaign leadership\",\n    \"marketing strategy\",\n    \"creative direction\",\n    \"content planning\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"canva\",\n    \"chatgpt\",\n    \"midjourney\",\n    \"notion\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"leadership\",\n    \"communication\",\n    \"storytelling\",\n    \"aesthetic sense\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"ad formats knowledge\",\n    \"consumer funnels\",\n    \"marketing metrics\",\n    \"campaign execution\",\n    \"jewelry industry knowledge\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": null\n}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1475,"output_tokens":261}},"recordId":"01JVA02K4HM2Q2MQR2FAQ5C16Q"}
{"modelInput":{"anthropic_version":"bedrock-2023-05-31","max_tokens":1024,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Extract the following details from the job description:\n\nEmployment Details:\n- Type of employment (FULL_TIME, PART_TIME, INTERNSHIP, CONTRACT, etc.)\n- Department (e.g., hr, marketing, sales, tech)\n- Company name\n- Salary range (minimum and maximum values)\n- Years of experience required (numeric values for min and max)\n- Notice period requirements (in months)\n\nSkills Requirements:\n- Core skills required for the role\n- Technical skills required (programming languages, software, etc.)\n- Soft skills and interpersonal abilities\n- Miscellaneous skills that don't fit other categories\n\nImportant Instructions:\n- Extract ONLY information explicitly mentioned in the job description\n- Do not infer or fabricate any details not present in the text\n- For type of employment, use UPPERCASE (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n- For department, use lowercase (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n- For company name, use UPPERCASE\n- For all skills, use lowercase format\n- If information for any field is not available, return an empty array or null as appropriate\n- If typeofEmployment or companyName are already present, do not update them\n\nHere is the job description:\n\n<div class=\"content-intro\"><p><strong>An Introduction to Codal</strong></p>\n<p>Codal is an award-winning web design and development consultancy that helps\nenterprise organizations solve complex problems and accelerate growth through\nelegant, data-driven digital solutions. Our areas of expertise include\napplication modernization, eCommerce, UX/UI design, product strategy, data\nanalytics, and artificial intelligence.&nbsp;</p> <p>At Codal, you’ll\ncollaborate with some of the most innovative organizations in the world and work\non cutting-edge technologies that push the boundaries of design and software\ndevelopment. You’ll also be part of a community that promotes long-term success,\nnot just for our clients but for each other. We’ll help you develop a\nprofessional roadmap that takes your career to new\nheights.&nbsp;</p></div><p></p> <p><strong>Who you’ll be working\nwith</strong></p> <p>We build the solutions dreamed up by the product and design\nteams. Our goal is to deliver working software every two weeks. We are a large\nteam that spans across three global offices, but we collaborate and integrate\nfront- and back-end components and interfaces to provide a user-centered\nexperience through web and mobile platforms.<br><br></p> <div><strong>What\nyou’ll be doing</strong></div> <ul> <li>Directly reporting and collaborating\nclosely with Engineering Managers</li> <li>Collaborating with the UX and UI\ndesign teams to produce seamless, robust, and innovative front-end user\nexperiences</li> <li>Managing multiple projects simultaneously, and be able to\naddress their specific needs and requirements at a moment’s notice</li> <li>Act\nas a subject matter expert in Shopify, specializing in all facets of the\nplatform</li> <li>Be on the front lines with other Front End Developers building\nout custom-tailored Shopify themes, altering pre-existing templates, and complex\ncustom solutions</li> <li>Collaborate closely Project Managers, Technical Leads,\nand clients to architect and craft Shopify websites</li> <li>Create compelling\nsolutions and functionality that inspire users and meet business goals</li>\n<li>Stay current on Shopify API changes and properly utilize them in your\nwork</li> <li>Understanding business needs that drive project features &amp;\nfunctions and provide internal consultation</li> </ul> <div><strong>What you’ll\nneed to be successful (Requirements)</strong></div> <ul> <li>Minimum 3+ years of\nexperience in front-end technology</li> <li>A minimum of 2 years of experience\nin eCommerce web development is must</li> <li>Strong knowledge of the Shopify\nplatform</li> <li>An ownership over project deliverables</li> <li>Expert\nknowledge of HTML and CSS nuances and proper semantics</li> <li>Expert skill set\nin JavaScript</li> <li>Solid understanding of progressive enhancement,\nresponsive design, accessibility and best UX/UI practices</li> <li>An expertise\nin Shopify theme development and customization</li> <li>Comfortability working\nwith graphQL, Storefront APIs and Liquid util-APIs</li> <li>Ability to work\nwithin a team environment where design and production are a collaborative\neffort</li> <li>Solid understanding of common Web accessibility patterns</li>\n<li>Experienced in integrating with REST APIs</li> <li>Background in page speed\nand rendering efficiency testing and remediation</li> <li>Excellent\ncommunication and interpersonal skills with team members and clients</li> </ul>\n<p></p> <p></p><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p>Note: Codal only communicates\nwith candidates through official @codal.com email addresses. We never request\npayment during the hiring process. Please be vigilant regarding recruitment\nscams.</p> <p><em>At Codal, we are committed to equal employment opportunities\nregardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual\norientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender, gender\nidentity or expression, or veteran status. We are proud to be an equal\nopportunity workplace.</em></p></div>\n\nReturn only the following JSON structure with extracted values. Do not provide any additional content, explanations, or details:\n\n{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n  \"department\": \"string\", // lowercase format (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n  \"companyName\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": number // in months, if mentioned\n}"}]}]},"modelOutput":{"id":"msg_bdrk_01Y86egvbvK5WS8DqGjU223W","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"FULL_TIME\",\n  \"department\": \"tech\",\n  \"companyName\": \"CODAL\",\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": null,\n    \"max\": null\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": 3,\n    \"max\": null\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"ecommerce web development\",\n    \"shopify platform expertise\",\n    \"front-end development\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"html\",\n    \"css\",\n    \"javascript\",\n    \"graphql\",\n    \"storefront apis\",\n    \"liquid util-apis\",\n    \"rest apis\",\n    \"shopify theme development\",\n    \"page speed optimization\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"communication\",\n    \"interpersonal skills\",\n    \"collaboration\",\n    \"project management\",\n    \"teamwork\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"progressive enhancement\",\n    \"responsive design\",\n    \"accessibility\",\n    \"ux/ui best practices\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": null\n}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1523,"output_tokens":287}},"recordId":"01JVA02K4X0WSHWF6A21ZPB1B7"}
{"modelInput":{"anthropic_version":"bedrock-2023-05-31","max_tokens":1024,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Extract the following details from the job description:\n\nEmployment Details:\n- Type of employment (FULL_TIME, PART_TIME, INTERNSHIP, CONTRACT, etc.)\n- Department (e.g., hr, marketing, sales, tech)\n- Company name\n- Salary range (minimum and maximum values)\n- Years of experience required (numeric values for min and max)\n- Notice period requirements (in months)\n\nSkills Requirements:\n- Core skills required for the role\n- Technical skills required (programming languages, software, etc.)\n- Soft skills and interpersonal abilities\n- Miscellaneous skills that don't fit other categories\n\nImportant Instructions:\n- Extract ONLY information explicitly mentioned in the job description\n- Do not infer or fabricate any details not present in the text\n- For type of employment, use UPPERCASE (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n- For department, use lowercase (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n- For company name, use UPPERCASE\n- For all skills, use lowercase format\n- If information for any field is not available, return an empty array or null as appropriate\n- If typeofEmployment or companyName are already present, do not update them\n\nHere is the job description:\n\nCOMPANY DESCRIPTION\n\nOrganizations everywhere struggle under the crushing costs and complexities of\n“solutions” that promise to simplify their lives. To create a better experience\nfor their customers and employees. To help them grow. Software is a choice that\ncan make or break a business. Create better or worse experiences. Propel or\nthrottle growth. Business software has become a blocker instead of ways to get\nwork done.\n\nThere’s another option. Freshworks. With a fresh vision for how the world works.\n\nAt Freshworks, we build uncomplicated service software that delivers exceptional\ncustomer and employee experiences. Our enterprise-grade solutions are powerful,\nyet easy to use, and quick to deliver results. Our people-first approach to AI\neliminates friction, making employees more effective and organizations more\nproductive. Over 72,000 companies, including Bridgestone, New Balance, Nucor,\nS&P Global, and Sony Music, trust Freshworks’ customer experience (CX) and\nemployee experience (EX) software to fuel customer loyalty and service\nefficiency. And, over 4,500 Freshworks employees make this possible, all around\nthe world.\n\nFresh vision. Real impact. Come build it with us.\n\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION\n\nThe Lead – IT Operations is accountable for designing, implementing, and\nmaintaining the organization’s infrastructure, including routers, switches,\nWi-Fi controllers, access points, load balancers, and firewalls. This role\ninvolves close collaboration with internal teams to ensure optimal performance,\nsecurity, and timely resolution of infrastructure-related issues.\n\nRole & Responsibilities:\n● Provide top notch support for any network issues ranging from implementation\nof new networks, troubleshooting outages for On-prem and remote networks\nbusiness users.\n● Handle level-2 support for Incidents, Changes and Service requests related to\nall Network & Security services\n● Technical support for networking such as: WAN and LAN connectivity, Link load\nbalancer, firewalls, wireless and security.\n● Develop and maintain network documentation, including network topology and\nconfiguration information.\n● Stay up to date with emerging trends and technologies in network & Security\nengineering.\n● Performing network maintenance and system upgrades including service packs,\npatches, hot fixes, and security configurations\n● Monitor system resource utilization, trending, and capacity planning for\nnetwork devices.\nDeployment of new Offices based on the requirement of the number of users for\nthe specific location.\n● Manage WiFi Controllers, Switches, Access Points (Ruckus) & Firewalls, such as\nPalo Alto\n● Remote access solution implementation and support such as IPSEC VPN & Remote\nVPN.\n● Hands-On executing the backup and restore of software and configuration\n● Must identify, resolve and replace malfunctioning hardware/software related\nincidents\n● Hands-on experience in defining, deploying/managing and troubleshooting the\nAAA mechanism for user authentication for device management\n● Understanding of DNS/DHCP.\n● Ability to work with vendor support to resolve Operational and Project\nchallenges.\n● Respond to and resolve alerts and tickets generated from the monitoring system\nin a timely fashion.\n● Create and Maintain record and maintain user support documentation (Knowledge\nBase) for Network & Security systems\n● Maintain accurate time and records in all service tickets as performed and\nensure the tickets get resolved with the given SLA timelines.\n● Communicate with customers/inter teams as needed regarding ticket progress,\nchanges or agreed outages.\n● Escalate service/incident requests that require L3 Engineer level support in a\ntimely fashion to prevent breach of SLA & Outage to business.\n● Work within a network team or with multiple stakeholders to implement and\nimprove best practices to enhance the user's experience and optimize the\noperation task.\n● Work with the Helpdesk Team to prioritize critical or high-impact network\nissue\n● Provide advanced troubleshooting support and guidance to ensure timely\nresolution\n● Act as the primary escalation point for complex network issues that are beyond\nthe scope of the Helpdesk Team.\n● Maintain clear and consistent communication with Helpdesk personnel during\nticket investigations and updates.\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\n● 8 -10 Years of relevant experience, Strong knowledge of Wireless/Wired LAN,\nWAN & Network Security infrastructure\n● Candidate will be responsible for, but not limited to, the following: (Must\nHave)\n○ Configuration, deployment, monitoring, troubleshooting, and analysis of Wired\n& Wireless network, WAN and Firewall infrastructure services\n○ Actively monitoring and reacting to real-time network conditions and leading\nimprovement efforts in support of monitoring, performance, and reporting.\n○ Well exposed to handle operation, deployment, and monitoring in the Wired &\nWireless, WAN and Firewall also good knowledge on standards such as wireless\nsecurity mechanisms, network design principles, firewall technology, and\nwireless network control systems, with a primary focus on\nRuckus/Aruba/Cisco/Palo Alto platforms.\n○ Hands-on experience implementing, upgrading/administering, and troubleshooting\nwireless controllers with an emphasis on Ruckus/Cisco/Palo Alto/Link Load\nBalancer devices.\n○ Should have good Debugging and Troubleshooting and log analysis skills\n○ Hands-on experience in defining, deploying/managing and troubleshooting the\nAuthentication, Authorization, Accounting mechanism for user authentication\n○ Hands-On experience in integration of analytics tools with WiFi / LAN/\nFirewall infrastructure for greater visibility and monitoring the traction\nhappening with networks.\n○ Excellent hands on knowledge of routing & switching technologies and\ntroubleshooting\n○ Hand-on experience & concept understanding in Firewalls like Palo Alto ,\nPRISMA & Cisco.\n\nSkills & Certifications\n● Must be well organized, responsible, and accountable\n● Must be detail-oriented, quick to learn and self-motivated\n● Strong understanding of TCP/IP networking and routing protocols.\n● Engineers must have good written, verbal and presentation skills to\ncollaborate successfully with team, vendors, and stakeholders.\n\n● Certification Requirements : (if any)\n○ CCNP Enterprise with network / security\n○ Palo Alto Certification (PCNSE)\n○ Wireless certification CWNA / CWNP\n\n● Educational qualifications:\nB.E. Degree, with any discipline.\n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\nAt Freshworks, we are creating a global workplace that enables everyone to find\ntheir true potential, purpose, and passion irrespective of their background,\ngender, race, sexual orientation, religion and ethnicity. We are committed to\nproviding equal opportunity for all and believe that diversity in the workplace\ncreates a more vibrant, richer work environment that advances the goals of our\nemployees, communities and the business.\n\nReturn only the following JSON structure with extracted values. Do not provide any additional content, explanations, or details:\n\n{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n  \"department\": \"string\", // lowercase format (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n  \"companyName\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": number // in months, if mentioned\n}"}]}]},"modelOutput":{"id":"msg_bdrk_01Pn2VqNTvWbAcVsLMeZoMr1","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"FULL_TIME\",\n  \"department\": \"it\",\n  \"companyName\": \"FRESHWORKS\",\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": null,\n    \"max\": null\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": 8,\n    \"max\": 10\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"network infrastructure management\",\n    \"wireless/wired lan\",\n    \"wan\",\n    \"network security infrastructure\",\n    \"network monitoring\",\n    \"network troubleshooting\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"tcp/ip\",\n    \"routing protocols\",\n    \"ruckus\",\n    \"aruba\",\n    \"cisco\",\n    \"palo alto\",\n    \"prisma\",\n    \"wifi controllers\",\n    \"switches\",\n    \"access points\",\n    \"firewalls\",\n    \"load balancers\",\n    \"ipsec vpn\",\n    \"remote vpn\",\n    \"dns/dhcp\",\n    \"aaa mechanism\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"written communication\",\n    \"verbal communication\",\n    \"presentation skills\",\n    \"detail-oriented\",\n    \"self-motivated\",\n    \"organized\",\n    \"responsible\",\n    \"accountable\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"documentation\",\n    \"vendor management\",\n    \"capacity planning\",\n    \"service level management\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": null\n}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2104,"output_tokens":371}},"recordId":"01JVA02K4YX6HFFHT5CMEDHBF1"}
{"modelInput":{"anthropic_version":"bedrock-2023-05-31","max_tokens":1024,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Extract the following details from the job description:\n\nEmployment Details:\n- Type of employment (FULL_TIME, PART_TIME, INTERNSHIP, CONTRACT, etc.)\n- Department (e.g., hr, marketing, sales, tech)\n- Company name\n- Salary range (minimum and maximum values)\n- Years of experience required (numeric values for min and max)\n- Notice period requirements (in months)\n\nSkills Requirements:\n- Core skills required for the role\n- Technical skills required (programming languages, software, etc.)\n- Soft skills and interpersonal abilities\n- Miscellaneous skills that don't fit other categories\n\nImportant Instructions:\n- Extract ONLY information explicitly mentioned in the job description\n- Do not infer or fabricate any details not present in the text\n- For type of employment, use UPPERCASE (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n- For department, use lowercase (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n- For company name, use UPPERCASE\n- For all skills, use lowercase format\n- If information for any field is not available, return an empty array or null as appropriate\n- If typeofEmployment or companyName are already present, do not update them\n\nHere is the job description:\n\nCOMPANY DESCRIPTION\n\n\"Why work for Accor?\nWe are far more than a worldwide leader. We welcome you as you are and you can\nfind a job and brand that matches your personality. We support you to grow and\nlearn every day, making sure that work brings purpose to your life, so that\nduring your journey with us, you can continue to explore Accor’s limitless\npossibilities.\nBy joining Accor, every chapter of your story is yours to write and together we\ncan imagine tomorrow's hospitality. Discover the life that awaits you at Accor,\nvisit https://careers.accor.com/\nDo what you love, care for the world, dare to challenge the status quo!\n#BELIMITLESS\"\n\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION\n\nGuest Service Associate-Housekeeping \nYou are at the heart of the hotel! As a Housekeeping Attendant, you will take\nownership of guest rooms, ensuring that our guests are provided with a clean,\ncomfortable space, and be a part of creating a memorable experience for them.\nWhat’s in it for you:\nEmployee benefit card offering discounted rates in Accor worldwide\nLearning programs through our Academies\nOpportunity to develop your talent and grow within your property and across the\nworld!\nAbility to make a difference through our Corporate Social Responsibility\nactivities, like Planet 21\nWhat you will be doing:\nClean all assigned guestrooms to standard\nTake initiative to add a personalized experience for the guest\nTake ownership of guests’ privacy and belongings, while ensuring exceptional\nservice\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\nYour experience and skills include:\nWarm and caring personality; previous housekeeping experience is an asset\nAbility to anticipate and focus attention on guest needs, being professional and\nwelcoming\nExcellent organizational skills and time management\n\nReturn only the following JSON structure with extracted values. Do not provide any additional content, explanations, or details:\n\n{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n  \"department\": \"string\", // lowercase format (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n  \"companyName\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": number // in months, if mentioned\n}"}]}]},"modelOutput":{"id":"msg_bdrk_019ojcPHmhRTpYFEGMgDYNgX","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"FULL_TIME\",\n  \"department\": \"housekeeping\",\n  \"companyName\": \"ACCOR\",\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": null,\n    \"max\": null\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": null,\n    \"max\": null\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"housekeeping\",\n    \"room cleaning\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"warm personality\",\n    \"caring personality\",\n    \"organizational skills\",\n    \"time management\",\n    \"attention to detail\",\n    \"guest service\",\n    \"professionalism\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [],\n  \"noticePeriod\": null\n}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":942,"output_tokens":200}},"recordId":"01JVA02K5JTJ8BRJAJ0D5D8PQ2"}
{"modelInput":{"anthropic_version":"bedrock-2023-05-31","max_tokens":1024,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Extract the following details from the job description:\n\nEmployment Details:\n- Type of employment (FULL_TIME, PART_TIME, INTERNSHIP, CONTRACT, etc.)\n- Department (e.g., hr, marketing, sales, tech)\n- Company name\n- Salary range (minimum and maximum values)\n- Years of experience required (numeric values for min and max)\n- Notice period requirements (in months)\n\nSkills Requirements:\n- Core skills required for the role\n- Technical skills required (programming languages, software, etc.)\n- Soft skills and interpersonal abilities\n- Miscellaneous skills that don't fit other categories\n\nImportant Instructions:\n- Extract ONLY information explicitly mentioned in the job description\n- Do not infer or fabricate any details not present in the text\n- For type of employment, use UPPERCASE (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n- For department, use lowercase (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n- For company name, use UPPERCASE\n- For all skills, use lowercase format\n- If information for any field is not available, return an empty array or null as appropriate\n- If typeofEmployment or companyName are already present, do not update them\n\nHere is the job description:\n\n<div class=\"content-intro\"><div>Harness is a high-growth company that is\ndisrupting the software delivery market. Our mission is to enable the 30 million\nsoftware developers in the world to deliver code to their users reliably,\nefficiently, securely and quickly, increasing customers’ pace of innovation\nwhile improving the developer experience. We offer solutions for every step of\nthe software delivery lifecycle to build, test, secure, deploy and manage\nreliability, feature flags and cloud costs. The Harness Software Delivery\nPlatform includes modules for CI, CD, Cloud Cost Management, Feature Flags,\nService Reliability Management, Security Testing Orchestration, Chaos\nEngineering, Software Engineering Insights and continues to expand at an\nincredibly fast pace.</div> <div>&nbsp;</div> <div>Harness is led by\ntechnologist and entrepreneur Jyoti Bansal, who founded AppDynamics and sold it\nto Cisco for $3.7B. We’re backed with $425M in venture financing from top-tier\nVC and strategic firms, including J.P. Morgan, Capital One Ventures, Citi\nVentures, ServiceNow, Splunk Ventures, Norwest Venture Partners, Adage Capital\nPartners, Balyasny Asset Management, Gaingels, Harmonic Growth Partners, Menlo\nVentures, IVP, Unusual Ventures, GV (formerly Google Ventures), Alkeon Capital,\nBattery Ventures, Sorenson Capital, Thomvest Ventures and Silicon Valley\nBank.</div></div><h3 class=\"\" data-start=\"360\" data-end=\"381\"><strong\ndata-start=\"364\" data-end=\"381\">Role Summary:</strong></h3> <p class=\"\"\ndata-start=\"383\" data-end=\"860\">We are seeking a detail-oriented and proactive\n<strong data-start=\"430\" data-end=\"457\">Procurement Coordinator</strong> to\nsupport our growing procurement operations. In this role, you will work closely\nwith the&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"550\" data-end=\"580\">Procurement\nManager</strong>, <strong data-start=\"582\" data-end=\"602\">Accounts\nPayable</strong>, and various internal departments to ensure smooth and timely\nexecution of procurement processes. You will be responsible for vendor\nonboarding, contract administration, procurement request tracking, and\nmaintaining compliance across procurement activities.</p> <h3 class=\"\"\ndata-start=\"867\" data-end=\"896\"><strong data-start=\"871\" data-end=\"896\">Key\nResponsibilities:</strong></h3> <ul data-start=\"898\" data-end=\"2139\"> <li\nclass=\"\" data-start=\"898\" data-end=\"1007\"> <p class=\"\" data-start=\"900\"\ndata-end=\"1007\">Support the <strong data-start=\"912\" data-end=\"942\">Senior\nProcurement Manager</strong> in managing procurement intake processes and vendor\nengagements.</p> </li> <li class=\"\" data-start=\"1008\" data-end=\"1132\"> <p\nclass=\"\" data-start=\"1010\" data-end=\"1132\">Oversee the end-to-end flow of\nprocurement requests, ensuring timely movement through the approval and\npurchasing process.</p> </li> <li class=\"\" data-start=\"1133\" data-end=\"1257\"> <p\nclass=\"\" data-start=\"1135\" data-end=\"1257\">Manage <strong data-start=\"1142\"\ndata-end=\"1163\">vendor onboarding</strong>, collect necessary documentation, and\nensure compliance with internal standards and policies.</p> </li> <li class=\"\"\ndata-start=\"1258\" data-end=\"1366\"> <p class=\"\" data-start=\"1260\"\ndata-end=\"1366\">Coordinate contract routing and signature collection, ensuring\ncontracts are executed and stored properly.</p> </li> <li class=\"\"\ndata-start=\"1367\" data-end=\"1475\"> <p class=\"\" data-start=\"1369\"\ndata-end=\"1475\">Maintain vendor master records, including tracking <strong\ndata-start=\"1420\" data-end=\"1435\">total spend</strong>, contract terms, and\nrenewal timelines.</p> </li> <li class=\"\" data-start=\"1476\" data-end=\"1619\"> <p\nclass=\"\" data-start=\"1478\" data-end=\"1619\">Act as a liaison for internal\ndepartments with vendors, responding to inquiries regarding contract status,\nterms, and procurement procedures.</p> </li> <li class=\"\" data-start=\"1620\"\ndata-end=\"1776\"> <p class=\"\" data-start=\"1622\" data-end=\"1776\">Collaborate with\n<strong data-start=\"1639\" data-end=\"1659\">Accounts Payable</strong> to resolve\ninvoice discrepancies and ensure invoices without purchase orders are routed and\ncorrected appropriately.</p> </li> <li class=\"\" data-start=\"1777\"\ndata-end=\"1933\"> <p class=\"\" data-start=\"1779\" data-end=\"1933\">Maintain and\nregularly update the <strong data-start=\"1813\" data-end=\"1848\">open Purchase\nOrder (PO) report</strong>, ensuring Accounting has accurate and up-to-date\ninformation for month-end accruals.</p> </li> <li class=\"\" data-start=\"1934\"\ndata-end=\"2037\"> <p class=\"\" data-start=\"1936\" data-end=\"2037\">Monitor\nprocurement dashboards and provide timely alerts on upcoming renewals and\nexpiring contracts.</p> </li> <li class=\"\" data-start=\"2038\" data-end=\"2139\"> <p\nclass=\"\" data-start=\"2040\" data-end=\"2139\">Perform any additional tasks or\nspecial projects as assigned by the <strong data-start=\"2108\"\ndata-end=\"2138\">Senior Procurement Manager</strong>.</p> </li> </ul> <h3\nclass=\"\" data-start=\"2146\" data-end=\"2169\"><strong data-start=\"2150\"\ndata-end=\"2169\">Qualifications:</strong></h3> <ul data-start=\"2171\"\ndata-end=\"3036\"> <li class=\"\" data-start=\"2171\" data-end=\"2293\"> <p class=\"\"\ndata-start=\"2173\" data-end=\"2293\">Minimum <strong data-start=\"2181\"\ndata-end=\"2192\">3 years</strong> of relevant office or administrative\nexperience, preferably in procurement or finance-related roles.</p> </li> <li\nclass=\"\" data-start=\"2294\" data-end=\"2396\"> <p class=\"\" data-start=\"2296\"\ndata-end=\"2396\">Proven experience in <strong data-start=\"2317\"\ndata-end=\"2338\">vendor management</strong> and coordinating with internal and\nexternal stakeholders.</p> </li> <li class=\"\" data-start=\"2397\" data-end=\"2521\">\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"2399\" data-end=\"2521\">Proficiency in <strong\ndata-start=\"2414\" data-end=\"2440\">Microsoft Office Suite</strong> (Word, Excel,\nPowerPoint); experience with procurement or ERP systems is a plus.</p> </li> <li\nclass=\"\" data-start=\"2522\" data-end=\"2649\"> <p class=\"\" data-start=\"2524\"\ndata-end=\"2649\">Excellent <strong data-start=\"2534\"\ndata-end=\"2559\">organizational skills</strong> with the ability to manage\nmultiple tasks and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment.</p> </li> <li\nclass=\"\" data-start=\"2650\" data-end=\"2777\"> <p class=\"\" data-start=\"2652\"\ndata-end=\"2777\">Strong <strong data-start=\"2659\" data-end=\"2702\">written and\nverbal communication skills</strong>; ability to communicate clearly and\nprofessionally with diverse audiences.</p> </li> <li class=\"\" data-start=\"2778\"\ndata-end=\"2864\"> <p class=\"\" data-start=\"2780\" data-end=\"2864\">Team player with\na collaborative mindset and the ability to work cross-functionally.</p> </li>\n<li class=\"\" data-start=\"2865\" data-end=\"2966\"> <p class=\"\" data-start=\"2867\"\ndata-end=\"2966\">High degree of <strong data-start=\"2882\"\ndata-end=\"2928\">integrity, discretion, and professionalism</strong> in handling\nconfidential information.</p> </li> <li class=\"\" data-start=\"2967\"\ndata-end=\"3036\"> <p class=\"\" data-start=\"2969\" data-end=\"3036\">Proactive,\nsolutions-oriented, and detail-focused approach to work.</p> </li> </ul> <p\nclass=\"\" data-start=\"3211\" data-end=\"3262\">&nbsp;</p><div\nclass=\"content-conclusion\"><h3>Harness in the news:</h3> <ul> <li><a\nhref=\"https://techcrunch.com/2024/05/14/after-surpassing-100m-in-arr-harness-labs-grabs-a-150m-line-of-credit/\"\ntarget=\"_parent\">Harness Grabs a $150m Line of Credit</a></li> <li><a\nhref=\"https://www.harness.io/blog/harness-to-acquire-split\"\ntarget=\"_parent\">Welcome Split!</a></li> <li><a class=\"postings-link\"\nhref=\"https://www.bizjournals.com/sanfrancisco/subscriber-only/2023/10/20/100-fastest-growing-private-companies-in-the-bay-area.html?b=1696980624%5E22314130\"\ntarget=\"_parent\">SF Business Times - 2024 - 100 Fastest-Growing Private\nCompanies in the Bay Area</a></li> <li><a\nhref=\"https://www.forbes.com/lists/americas-best-startup-employers/?sh=6f2a8dfd2ad7\"\ntarget=\"_parent\">Forbes - 2024 America's Best Startup Employers</a></li> <li><a\nhref=\"https://www.bizjournals.com/sanfrancisco/event/170332/2024/fastest-growing-private-companies-awards\"\ntarget=\"_parent\">SF Business Times - 2024 Fastest Growing Private Companies\nAwards</a></li> <li><a\nhref=\"https://www.fastcompany.com/best-workplaces-for-innovators/list?utm_medium=DSMN8&amp;utm_source=LinkedIn\"\ntarget=\"_parent\">Fast Co - 2024 100 Best Workplaces for Innovators</a></li>\n</ul> <p>All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment\nwithout regard to race, color, religion, sex or national origin.<br><br></p>\n<p><strong>Note on Fraudulent Recruiting/Offers</strong></p> <p>We have become\naware that there may be fraudulent recruiting attempts being made by people\nposing as representatives of Harness. These scams may involve fake job postings,\nunsolicited emails, or messages claiming to be from our recruiters or hiring\nmanagers.&nbsp;</p> <p>Please note, we do not ask for sensitive or financial\ninformation via chat, text, or social media, and any email communications will\ncome from the domain @harness.io. Additionally, Harness will never ask for any\npayment, fee to be paid, or purchases to be made by a job applicant. All\napplicants are encouraged to apply directly to our open jobs via our website.\nInterviews are generally conducted via Zoom video conference unless the\ncandidate requests other accommodations.</p> <p>If you believe that you have\nbeen the target of an interview/offer scam by someone posing as a representative\nof Harness, please do not provide any personal or financial information and\ncontact us immediately at&nbsp;<a\nhref=\"mailto:security@harness.io\">security@harness.io</a>. You can also find\nadditional information about this type of scam and report any fraudulent\nemployment offers via the Federal Trade Commission’s website (<a\nhref=\"https://consumer.ftc.gov/articles/job-scams)\">https://consumer.ftc.gov/articles/job-scams)</a>,\nor you can contact your local law enforcement agency.</p></div>\n\nReturn only the following JSON structure with extracted values. Do not provide any additional content, explanations, or details:\n\n{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n  \"department\": \"string\", // lowercase format (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n  \"companyName\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": number // in months, if mentioned\n}"}]}]},"modelOutput":{"id":"msg_bdrk_01LqhXkf3QHLKFWQaanvxVbG","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"FULL_TIME\",\n  \"department\": \"procurement\",\n  \"companyName\": \"HARNESS\",\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": null,\n    \"max\": null\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": 3,\n    \"max\": null\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"vendor management\",\n    \"contract administration\",\n    \"procurement processes\",\n    \"vendor onboarding\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"microsoft office suite\",\n    \"erp systems\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"organizational skills\",\n    \"written and verbal communication skills\",\n    \"integrity\",\n    \"discretion\",\n    \"professionalism\",\n    \"team player\",\n    \"collaborative mindset\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"detail-oriented\",\n    \"proactive\",\n    \"solutions-oriented\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": null\n}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3475,"output_tokens":254}},"recordId":"01JVA02K63J3NMG3D2X8MA4VV2"}
{"modelInput":{"anthropic_version":"bedrock-2023-05-31","max_tokens":1024,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Extract the following details from the job description:\n\nEmployment Details:\n- Type of employment (FULL_TIME, PART_TIME, INTERNSHIP, CONTRACT, etc.)\n- Department (e.g., hr, marketing, sales, tech)\n- Company name\n- Salary range (minimum and maximum values)\n- Years of experience required (numeric values for min and max)\n- Notice period requirements (in months)\n\nSkills Requirements:\n- Core skills required for the role\n- Technical skills required (programming languages, software, etc.)\n- Soft skills and interpersonal abilities\n- Miscellaneous skills that don't fit other categories\n\nImportant Instructions:\n- Extract ONLY information explicitly mentioned in the job description\n- Do not infer or fabricate any details not present in the text\n- For type of employment, use UPPERCASE (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n- For department, use lowercase (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n- For company name, use UPPERCASE\n- For all skills, use lowercase format\n- If information for any field is not available, return an empty array or null as appropriate\n- If typeofEmployment or companyName are already present, do not update them\n\nHere is the job description:\n\nCOMPANY DESCRIPTION\n\nExperian is a global data and technology company, powering opportunities for\npeople and businesses around the world. We help to redefine lending practices,\nuncover and prevent fraud, simplify healthcare, create marketing solutions, and\ngain deeper insights into the automotive market, all using our unique\ncombination of data, analytics and software. We also assist millions of people\nto realize their financial goals and help them save time and money.\n\nWe operate across a range of markets, from financial services to healthcare,\nautomotive, agribusiness, insurance, and many more industry segments.\n\nWe invest in people and new advanced technologies to unlock the power of data.\nAs a FTSE 100 Index company listed on the London Stock Exchange (EXPN), we have\na team of 22,500 people across 32 countries. Our corporate headquarters are in\nDublin, Ireland. Learn more at experianplc.com.\n\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION\n\nWe are looking for an individual to lead our product development team. This\nperson must be a self-starter and not be afraid to roll-up their sleeves as a\nplayer-coach. The ideal candidate will have customer support application\nexperience and the ability to easily communicate across all levels of the\norganization. This individual will be part of the CIS technology team and report\nto the Senior Director of Product Development.  \n\n * Oversees and provides technical direction to software engineering team(s),\n   recruits and retains talented engineers, develops, monitors, and controls\n   resource allocation plans \n\n * Delivers complex products involving both file extracts, batch interactions\n   and interactive technologies \n\n * Applies expert knowledge of applicable software development tools and\n   application hosting platforms \n\n * Applies expertise in software system design: scalability, reliability,\n   extensibility, usability \n\n * Distills complex ideas into understandable communication for a wide audience \n\n * Manages relationships with strategic partners/clients for product releases\n   and system issues \n\n * Coordinates engagement of software engineering teams in production support\n   within their application domain \n\n * Partners with scrum masters to develop, monitor, and control software\n   delivery plans \n\n * Partners with Product Management to develop technology and product roadmaps \n\n * Provides guidance for best practice in security for software development \n\n * Coordinates activities and prepares artifacts for internal and external\n   auditors/customers \n\n * Defines guardrails in development to uphold regulatory compliance \n\n * Promotes consistent agile practices across teams, reduces delivery time and\n   improves quality of work \n\n \n\n *  \n\n \n\n \n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\nQualifications\n\n * Bachelor's degree in Engineering, Computer Science, or equivalent experience\n   required. \n * Masters strongly preferred. \n * 8-10 years overall work experience, 3+ years’ experience in direct team\n   management Knowledge of a broad range of both commercial and opensource\n   solutions - Java/J2EE, Spring Boot, python, CICD, RxJava, JS \n * Experience with modern technology stack in the areas of Cloud, API,\n   Microservices \n * Experience with AWS in a development role is preferred Agile/Scrum Expertise\n   required \n * Established record of strong technical leadership in a high-performing\n   technology company.\n * Excellent communication skills and a deep understanding of\n   technology Experience in preparing materials and presenting to wider\n   audiences, translating technologies into products Proven success in\n   developing teams to deliver and demonstrated engineering excellence \n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\nOur uniqueness is that we celebrate yours. Experian's culture and people are\nimportant differentiators. We take our people agenda very seriously and focus on\nwhat matters; DEI, work/life balance, development, authenticity, collaboration,\nwellness, reward & recognition, volunteering... the list goes on. Experian's\npeople first approach is award-winning; World's Best Workplaces™ 2024 (Fortune\nTop 25), Great Place To Work™ in 24 countries, and Glassdoor Best Places to Work\n2024 to name a few. Check out Experian Life on social or our Careers Site to\nunderstand why.\n\nExperian is proud to be an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action employer.\nInnovation is an important part of Experian's DNA and practices, and our diverse\nworkforce drives our success. Everyone can succeed at Experian and bring their\nwhole self to work, irrespective of their gender, ethnicity, religion, colour,\nsexuality, physical ability or age. If you have a disability or special need\nthat requires accommodation, please let us know at the earliest opportunity.\n\n\n\nExperian Careers - Creating a better tomorrow together\n\nFind out what its like to work for Experian by clicking here\n[https://www.experian.com/careers/]\n\nReturn only the following JSON structure with extracted values. Do not provide any additional content, explanations, or details:\n\n{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n  \"department\": \"string\", // lowercase format (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n  \"companyName\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": number // in months, if mentioned\n}"}]}]},"modelOutput":{"id":"msg_bdrk_016sgwPiz4s6V2E8oiSnH9T3","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"FULL_TIME\",\n  \"department\": \"tech\",\n  \"companyName\": \"EXPERIAN\",\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": null,\n    \"max\": null\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": 8,\n    \"max\": 10\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"software system design\",\n    \"product development\",\n    \"team management\",\n    \"agile/scrum expertise\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"java/j2ee\",\n    \"spring boot\",\n    \"python\",\n    \"cicd\",\n    \"rxjava\",\n    \"js\",\n    \"aws\",\n    \"cloud\",\n    \"api\",\n    \"microservices\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"communication\",\n    \"leadership\",\n    \"relationship management\",\n    \"presentation skills\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"technical direction\",\n    \"resource allocation\",\n    \"product roadmap planning\",\n    \"security best practices\",\n    \"regulatory compliance\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": null\n}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1635,"output_tokens":293}},"recordId":"01JVA02K67N00X4PQE70HFYTRW"}
{"modelInput":{"anthropic_version":"bedrock-2023-05-31","max_tokens":1024,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Extract the following details from the job description:\n\nEmployment Details:\n- Type of employment (FULL_TIME, PART_TIME, INTERNSHIP, CONTRACT, etc.)\n- Department (e.g., hr, marketing, sales, tech)\n- Company name\n- Salary range (minimum and maximum values)\n- Years of experience required (numeric values for min and max)\n- Notice period requirements (in months)\n\nSkills Requirements:\n- Core skills required for the role\n- Technical skills required (programming languages, software, etc.)\n- Soft skills and interpersonal abilities\n- Miscellaneous skills that don't fit other categories\n\nImportant Instructions:\n- Extract ONLY information explicitly mentioned in the job description\n- Do not infer or fabricate any details not present in the text\n- For type of employment, use UPPERCASE (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n- For department, use lowercase (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n- For company name, use UPPERCASE\n- For all skills, use lowercase format\n- If information for any field is not available, return an empty array or null as appropriate\n- If typeofEmployment or companyName are already present, do not update them\n\nHere is the job description:\n\nCOMPANY DESCRIPTION\n\nOrganizations everywhere struggle under the crushing costs and complexities of\n“solutions” that promise to simplify their lives. To create a better experience\nfor their customers and employees. To help them grow. Software is a choice that\ncan make or break a business. Create better or worse experiences. Propel or\nthrottle growth. Business software has become a blocker instead of ways to get\nwork done.\n\nThere’s another option. Freshworks. With a fresh vision for how the world works.\n\nAt Freshworks, we build uncomplicated service software that delivers exceptional\ncustomer and employee experiences. Our enterprise-grade solutions are powerful,\nyet easy to use, and quick to deliver results. Our people-first approach to AI\neliminates friction, making employees more effective and organizations more\nproductive. Over 72,000 companies, including Bridgestone, New Balance, Nucor,\nS&P Global, and Sony Music, trust Freshworks’ customer experience (CX) and\nemployee experience (EX) software to fuel customer loyalty and service\nefficiency. And, over 4,500 Freshworks employees make this possible, all around\nthe world.\n\nFresh vision. Real impact. Come build it with us.\n\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION\n\nThe Manager – IT Network and Security will lead the planning, deployment, and\nsupport of network infrastructure and security operations across the enterprise.\nThis role requires hands-on technical knowledge as well as leadership\ncapabilities to manage a team of network and security engineers. The individual\nwill be responsible for maintaining secure, reliable, and high-performance\nconnectivity across on-premise and cloud environments.\n\nRole & Responsibilities:\n● Experience in Network Design, Implementation and support\n● Responsible for creating High level Network design, Low level design,\nImplementation Plan, migration plan, testing plan for the new projects\n● Validating the existing design and provide recommendations for optimization\n● Responsible for troubleshooting and fixing Major Network issues (Priority\nMedium to Critical)\n● Participate in Major/Minor Incident Management Calls and provide\nsolution/update on a timely manner\n● Supervise and mentor a team of network and security engineers and analysts.\n● Technical co-ordination with the OEM support in the event of any Technology\nassistance ·\n● Update Training and Support documentation\n● Manage end-to-end enterprise networking (LAN, WAN, Wireless & Firewall)\n● Coordinate with cross-functional teams to support business and IT initiatives.\n● Oversee performance monitoring, fault management, and capacity planning.\n● Lead lifecycle management of network hardware and software.\n● Understand and document the Current Mode of Operations (CMO)\n● Security patches and updates to network devices and firewalls to address\nvulnerabilities\n● Collecting and analysing logs from network devices and firewalls to identify\npotential security events\n● Create and maintain detailed network diagrams, configuration standards, and\nSOPs\n● Work with the Helpdesk Team to prioritize critical or high-impact network\nissues\n● Act as the primary escalation point for complex network issues that are beyond\nthe scope of the Helpdesk Team.\n● Maintain clear and consistent communication with Helpdesk personnel during\nticket investigations and updates.\n● Provide advanced troubleshooting support and guidance to ensure timely\nresolution\n● Share relevant documentation and standard operating procedures (SOPs) with the\nIT Helpdesk Team.\n● Conduct periodic knowledge transfer sessions to enhance the Helpdesk Team’s\ncapability in handling recurring or common network issues\n● Participate in regular sync-ups or reviews to analyze ticket trends, root\ncauses, and process improvements.\n● Ensure that resolutions and network-related knowledge base articles are\nproperly documented.\n● Contribute to reports on ticket resolution times, recurring issues, and\nrecommendations for network improvements.\n● Act as the main liaison between IT operations and the GRC team to align on\nsecurity posture, risk mitigation, and compliance.\n● Contribute to internal risk assessments, control validations, and audit\nreadiness while ensuring IT practices align with GRC-defined strategies\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\n● Strong knowledge of Wireless/Wired LAN, WAN & Network Security infrastructure\n● 10 - 15 Years relevant experince,13+ years of experience in network and\nsecurity, with 2+ years in a senior technical lead role\n● Candidate will be responsible for, but not limited to, the following: (Must\nHave)\n○ Configuration, deployment, monitoring, troubleshooting, and analysis of Wired\n& Wireless network, WAN and Firewall infrastructure services\n○ Actively monitoring and reacting to real-time network conditions and leading\nimprovement efforts in support of monitoring, performance, and reporting.\n○ Well exposed to handle operation, deployment, and monitoring in the Wired &\nWireless, WAN and Firewall also good knowledge on standards such as wireless\nsecurity mechanisms, network design principles, firewall technology, and\nwireless network control systems, with a primary focus on\nRuckus/Aruba/Cisco/Palo Alto platforms.\n○ Hands-on experience implementing, upgrading/administering, and troubleshooting\nwireless controllers with an emphasis on Ruckus/Cisco/Palo Alto/Link Load\nBalancer devices.\n○ Should have good Debugging and Troubleshooting and log analysis skills\n○ Hands-on experience in defining, deploying/managing and troubleshooting the\nAuthentication, Authorization, Accounting mechanism for user authentication\n○ Hands-On experience in integration of analytics tools with WiFi / LAN/\nFirewall infrastructure for greater visibility and monitoring the traction\nhappening with networks\n○ Excellent hands on knowledge of routing & switching technologies and\ntroubleshooting.\n○ Hand-on experience & concept understanding in Firewalls like Palo Alto & VPN\nCloud/ PRISMA\n○ Strong troubleshooting and problem-solving skills ○ Ability to design complex\nnetwork architectures\n○ Experience with centralized network monitoring and management systems\n\nSkills & Certifications\n● Exceptional leadership and team management capabilities\n● Strong communication skills\n● Strategic thinking and forward-planning mindset\n● Excellent project management skills\n● Ability to manage complex & distributed network environments\n● Certification Requirements : (if any)\n○ CCDP Enterprise with Network / Security\n○ Palo Alto Certification (PCNSE)\n○ Wireless certification CWNA / CWNP ○ ITIL and PMP (for operational/process\nalignment)\n\n● Educational qualifications: B.E. Degree, with any discipline.\n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\nAt Freshworks, we are creating a global workplace that enables everyone to find\ntheir true potential, purpose, and passion irrespective of their background,\ngender, race, sexual orientation, religion and ethnicity. We are committed to\nproviding equal opportunity for all and believe that diversity in the workplace\ncreates a more vibrant, richer work environment that advances the goals of our\nemployees, communities and the business.\n\nReturn only the following JSON structure with extracted values. Do not provide any additional content, explanations, or details:\n\n{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n  \"department\": \"string\", // lowercase format (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n  \"companyName\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": number // in months, if mentioned\n}"}]}]},"modelOutput":{"id":"msg_bdrk_01KviMjfLjTrSBUwestJHnHU","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"FULL_TIME\",\n  \"department\": \"it\",\n  \"companyName\": \"FRESHWORKS\",\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": null,\n    \"max\": null\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": 10,\n    \"max\": 15\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"network design\",\n    \"network implementation\",\n    \"network security\",\n    \"infrastructure management\",\n    \"enterprise networking\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"lan\",\n    \"wan\",\n    \"wireless networks\",\n    \"firewalls\",\n    \"ruckus\",\n    \"aruba\",\n    \"cisco\",\n    \"palo alto\",\n    \"routing\",\n    \"switching\",\n    \"vpn cloud\",\n    \"prisma\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"leadership\",\n    \"team management\",\n    \"communication\",\n    \"strategic thinking\",\n    \"project management\",\n    \"problem solving\",\n    \"mentoring\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"incident management\",\n    \"documentation\",\n    \"troubleshooting\",\n    \"risk assessment\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": null\n}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2117,"output_tokens":315}},"recordId":"01JVA02K692C7QHHZ3ZFMSMQZN"}
{"modelInput":{"anthropic_version":"bedrock-2023-05-31","max_tokens":1024,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Extract the following details from the job description:\n\nEmployment Details:\n- Type of employment (FULL_TIME, PART_TIME, INTERNSHIP, CONTRACT, etc.)\n- Department (e.g., hr, marketing, sales, tech)\n- Company name\n- Salary range (minimum and maximum values)\n- Years of experience required (numeric values for min and max)\n- Notice period requirements (in months)\n\nSkills Requirements:\n- Core skills required for the role\n- Technical skills required (programming languages, software, etc.)\n- Soft skills and interpersonal abilities\n- Miscellaneous skills that don't fit other categories\n\nImportant Instructions:\n- Extract ONLY information explicitly mentioned in the job description\n- Do not infer or fabricate any details not present in the text\n- For type of employment, use UPPERCASE (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n- For department, use lowercase (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n- For company name, use UPPERCASE\n- For all skills, use lowercase format\n- If information for any field is not available, return an empty array or null as appropriate\n- If typeofEmployment or companyName are already present, do not update them\n\nHere is the job description:\n\nCOMPANY DESCRIPTION\n\nEvery institution values excellence. What matters most is why.\nGriffith was created to be a different type of university.  You’ll find we’re\nabout leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of\neducation. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll\nachieve them.\n\nWhy? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe\nand from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and\nchallenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.\n\nPlaying a critical role in supporting Griffith's ambitions is Griffith\nEnterprise [https://www.griffith.edu.au/griffith-enterprise], the university’s\ndedicated commercialisation office, managing and commercialising the\nuniversities intellectual property and research expertise. Griffith Enterprise’s\nmission is to manage and facilitate the commercialisation of intellectual\nproperty and research excellence from Griffith University researchers via the\nmost appropriate commercialisation pathway, ensuring optimum outcomes for all of\nour partners whilst protecting and enhancing the reputation of the university.\nBy translating and commercialising ground-breaking technologies and research\nexcellence, empowering a culture of collaboration, and prioritising our\npartner’s needs we help them achieve their strategic ambitions and generate\nglobal impact.\n\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION\n\nAs the Commercialisation Manager (Medtech) you will be responsible for\nidentifying, developing and leading commercialisation opportunities,\ntransactions and strategic initiatives in the area of Medtech as part of the\nLife Science team focussing on commercialisation of technologies in the Medtech\narea such as medical devices and digital health.\n\nYou will work closely with Griffith researchers to identify and assess potential\nnew intellectual property and through business development activities negotiate\ncommercialisation transactions such as licences, start-ups, research agreements\nto take the research to the market.\n\nYou will play a key role in advancing commercialisation awareness and skills\nacross the University and, along with key Griffith staff, engaging with partners\nto help shape strategic partnerships.  As a senior member of the team, you will\nlead all aspects of the commercialisation and IP management process, from\nearly-stage research to the negotiations of deals and establishing start-up\ncompanies.\n\nAbout you\nTo be successful in this role you will hold a postgraduate degree and 5+ years’\nexperience in a similar role and a strong track record of success in\nidentifying, managing and commercialising intellectual property in the field of\nMedtech/digital health based research through licences, research collaborations\nand/or start-ups.\n\nYou will also have technical knowledge in a relevant area of Medtech/digital\nhealth and demonstrated business development expertise and a track record will\nbe required. Your ability to deal with complex situations and communicate\nclearly will be an asset to the team.\n\nDemonstrated skills required to assess early-stage technologies and understand\nintellectual property (IP) management and protection, including patents and\nother forms of IP; identify and negotiate commercial opportunities; and a proven\nability to scope, pitch and negotiate commercialisation transactions are\nessential.\n\nYou will need to be a self-starter and team player. You will be given the\nautonomy and responsibility to make a significant contribution to Griffith\nEnterprise and the University.\n\nWhat we can offer\nThis is a continuing, full-time position and will be primarily based at Griffith\nUniversity’s Brisbane South (Nathan) or Gold Coast. As Griffith is a multi-site\nUniversity you may be required to work across other locations.  Griffith\nUniversity’s campuses are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera,\nJagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples.\n\nSalary Range\nA competitive remuneration package will be negotiated with the successful\napplicant.\n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\nWhy Griffith?\nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to\ncreate a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer:\n\n * Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities\n * Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work\n   environment\n * Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts\n * Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading\n * Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff\n   assistance scheme\n\nHow to apply\nAt Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for\nall - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any\naccommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to\nparticipate fully in our recruitment experience.\n\nGriffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage\nAboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply.\nFor more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion\n[https://www.griffith.edu.au/equity#:~:text=At%20Griffith%20we%20understand%20that,safe%2C%20supportive%20and%20productive%20environment]\npage. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against\nall forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s\nModern Slavery Policy\n[https://www.griffith.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0037/1687357/modern-slavery-policy-2022.pdf].\n\nPlease submit your application online and ensure it includes the following:\n\n * A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to\n   the About you section above and the position description\n   [https://c.smartrecruiters.com/sr-company-attachments-prod-aws-dc5/6270a42b9da2f23e08f16ddd/44151a6a-c3a9-4354-90e6-c6976f36aa2a?r=s3-eu-central-1])\n * Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details\n * A non-confidential deal sheet highlighting your deal track record\n\nApplicants must have unrestricted working rights for the duration of the\nappointment. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position.\n\nSuccessful candidates may be subject to a criminal history check.\n\nFor further information specifically about this role, Dr Mark Ashton, Director,\nGriffith Enterprise on [email protected]\n[/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#e08792898686899488858e9485929092899385a087928986869488ce858495ce8195].\n\nFor application support, please contact People Services on +61 (0) 7 3735 4011\nquoting reference number REF7589L.\n\nClosing date:  Monday, 26 May 2025 at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be\nsubmitted online.\n\nPlease allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application\nupdate.\n\nReturn only the following JSON structure with extracted values. Do not provide any additional content, explanations, or details:\n\n{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n  \"department\": \"string\", // lowercase format (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n  \"companyName\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": number // in months, if mentioned\n}"}]}]},"modelOutput":{"id":"msg_bdrk_01CniJfAC58nGcB5ahLXnc64","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"FULL_TIME\",\n  \"department\": \"commercialisation\",\n  \"companyName\": \"GRIFFITH UNIVERSITY\",\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": null,\n    \"max\": null\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": 5,\n    \"max\": null\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"intellectual property management\",\n    \"commercialisation\",\n    \"business development\",\n    \"deal negotiation\",\n    \"technology assessment\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"medtech\",\n    \"digital health\",\n    \"patent management\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"communication\",\n    \"leadership\",\n    \"team player\",\n    \"self-starter\",\n    \"negotiation\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"research collaboration\",\n    \"strategic partnerships\",\n    \"stakeholder management\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": null\n}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2106,"output_tokens":251}},"recordId":"01JVA02K6Q6BQ0BD3E9EMQ5AQ8"}
{"modelInput":{"anthropic_version":"bedrock-2023-05-31","max_tokens":1024,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Extract the following details from the job description:\n\nEmployment Details:\n- Type of employment (FULL_TIME, PART_TIME, INTERNSHIP, CONTRACT, etc.)\n- Department (e.g., hr, marketing, sales, tech)\n- Company name\n- Salary range (minimum and maximum values)\n- Years of experience required (numeric values for min and max)\n- Notice period requirements (in months)\n\nSkills Requirements:\n- Core skills required for the role\n- Technical skills required (programming languages, software, etc.)\n- Soft skills and interpersonal abilities\n- Miscellaneous skills that don't fit other categories\n\nImportant Instructions:\n- Extract ONLY information explicitly mentioned in the job description\n- Do not infer or fabricate any details not present in the text\n- For type of employment, use UPPERCASE (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n- For department, use lowercase (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n- For company name, use UPPERCASE\n- For all skills, use lowercase format\n- If information for any field is not available, return an empty array or null as appropriate\n- If typeofEmployment or companyName are already present, do not update them\n\nHere is the job description:\n\nCOMPANY DESCRIPTION\n\nEvery institution values excellence. What matters most is why.\nGriffith was created to be a different type of university.  You’ll find we’re\nabout leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of\neducation. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll\nachieve them.\n\nWhy? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe\nand from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and\nchallenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.\n\nPlaying a critical role in supporting Griffith's ambitions is Griffith\nEnterprise [https://www.griffith.edu.au/griffith-enterprise], the university’s\ndedicated commercialisation office, managing and commercialising the\nuniversities intellectual property and research expertise. Griffith Enterprise’s\nmission is to manage and facilitate the commercialisation of intellectual\nproperty and research excellence from Griffith University researchers via the\nmost appropriate commercialisation pathway, ensuring optimum outcomes for all of\nour partners whilst protecting and enhancing the reputation of the university.\nBy translating and commercialising ground-breaking technologies and research\nexcellence, empowering a culture of collaboration, and prioritising our\npartner’s needs we help them achieve their strategic ambitions and generate\nglobal impact.\n\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION\n\nAs the Commercialisation Manager (Medtech) you will be responsible for\nidentifying, developing and leading commercialisation opportunities,\ntransactions and strategic initiatives in the area of Medtech as part of the\nLife Science team focussing on commercialisation of technologies in the Medtech\narea such as medical devices and digital health.\n\nYou will work closely with Griffith researchers to identify and assess potential\nnew intellectual property and through business development activities negotiate\ncommercialisation transactions such as licences, start-ups, research agreements\nto take the research to the market.\n\nYou will play a key role in advancing commercialisation awareness and skills\nacross the University and, along with key Griffith staff, engaging with partners\nto help shape strategic partnerships.  As a senior member of the team, you will\nlead all aspects of the commercialisation and IP management process, from\nearly-stage research to the negotiations of deals and establishing start-up\ncompanies.\n\nAbout you\nTo be successful in this role you will hold a postgraduate degree and 5+ years’\nexperience in a similar role and a strong track record of success in\nidentifying, managing and commercialising intellectual property in the field of\nMedtech/digital health based research through licences, research collaborations\nand/or start-ups.\n\nYou will also have technical knowledge in a relevant area of Medtech/digital\nhealth and demonstrated business development expertise and a track record will\nbe required. Your ability to deal with complex situations and communicate\nclearly will be an asset to the team.\n\nDemonstrated skills required to assess early-stage technologies and understand\nintellectual property (IP) management and protection, including patents and\nother forms of IP; identify and negotiate commercial opportunities; and a proven\nability to scope, pitch and negotiate commercialisation transactions are\nessential.\n\nYou will need to be a self-starter and team player. You will be given the\nautonomy and responsibility to make a significant contribution to Griffith\nEnterprise and the University.\n\nWhat we can offer\nThis is a continuing, full-time position and will be primarily based at Griffith\nUniversity’s Brisbane South (Nathan) or Gold Coast. As Griffith is a multi-site\nUniversity you may be required to work across other locations.  Griffith\nUniversity’s campuses are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera,\nJagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples.\n\nSalary Range\nA competitive remuneration package will be negotiated with the successful\napplicant.\n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\nWhy Griffith?\nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to\ncreate a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer:\n\n * Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities\n * Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work\n   environment\n * Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts\n * Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading\n * Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff\n   assistance scheme\n\nHow to apply\nAt Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for\nall - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any\naccommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to\nparticipate fully in our recruitment experience.\n\nGriffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage\nAboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply.\nFor more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion\n[https://www.griffith.edu.au/equity#:~:text=At%20Griffith%20we%20understand%20that,safe%2C%20supportive%20and%20productive%20environment]\npage. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against\nall forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s\nModern Slavery Policy\n[https://www.griffith.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0037/1687357/modern-slavery-policy-2022.pdf].\n\nPlease submit your application online and ensure it includes the following:\n\n * A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to\n   the About you section above and the position description\n   [https://c.smartrecruiters.com/sr-company-attachments-prod-aws-dc5/6270a42b9da2f23e08f16ddd/44151a6a-c3a9-4354-90e6-c6976f36aa2a?r=s3-eu-central-1])\n * Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details\n * A non-confidential deal sheet highlighting your deal track record\n\nApplicants must have unrestricted working rights for the duration of the\nappointment. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position.\n\nSuccessful candidates may be subject to a criminal history check.\n\nFor further information specifically about this role, Dr Mark Ashton, Director,\nGriffith Enterprise on [email protected]\n[/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#abccd9c2cdcdc2dfc3cec5dfced9dbd9c2d8ceebccd9c2cdcddfc385cecfde85cade].\n\nFor application support, please contact People Services on +61 (0) 7 3735 4011\nquoting reference number REF7589L.\n\nClosing date:  Monday, 26 May 2025 at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be\nsubmitted online.\n\nPlease allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application\nupdate.\n\nReturn only the following JSON structure with extracted values. Do not provide any additional content, explanations, or details:\n\n{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n  \"department\": \"string\", // lowercase format (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n  \"companyName\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": number // in months, if mentioned\n}"}]}]},"modelOutput":{"id":"msg_bdrk_01JXafkFtYrktWZsDsmVmUQ2","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"FULL_TIME\",\n  \"department\": \"commercialisation\",\n  \"companyName\": \"GRIFFITH UNIVERSITY\",\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": null,\n    \"max\": null\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": 5,\n    \"max\": null\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"intellectual property management\",\n    \"commercialisation\",\n    \"business development\",\n    \"medtech expertise\",\n    \"digital health expertise\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"patent management\",\n    \"ip protection\",\n    \"medical devices knowledge\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"communication\",\n    \"negotiation\",\n    \"self-starter\",\n    \"team player\",\n    \"leadership\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"deal negotiation\",\n    \"research collaboration\",\n    \"strategic partnership building\",\n    \"technology assessment\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": null\n}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2123,"output_tokens":260}},"recordId":"01JVA02K6RKVJG2P6JQAWH2WBA"}
{"modelInput":{"anthropic_version":"bedrock-2023-05-31","max_tokens":1024,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Extract the following details from the job description:\n\nEmployment Details:\n- Type of employment (FULL_TIME, PART_TIME, INTERNSHIP, CONTRACT, etc.)\n- Department (e.g., hr, marketing, sales, tech)\n- Company name\n- Salary range (minimum and maximum values)\n- Years of experience required (numeric values for min and max)\n- Notice period requirements (in months)\n\nSkills Requirements:\n- Core skills required for the role\n- Technical skills required (programming languages, software, etc.)\n- Soft skills and interpersonal abilities\n- Miscellaneous skills that don't fit other categories\n\nImportant Instructions:\n- Extract ONLY information explicitly mentioned in the job description\n- Do not infer or fabricate any details not present in the text\n- For type of employment, use UPPERCASE (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n- For department, use lowercase (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n- For company name, use UPPERCASE\n- For all skills, use lowercase format\n- If information for any field is not available, return an empty array or null as appropriate\n- If typeofEmployment or companyName are already present, do not update them\n\nHere is the job description:\n\nCOMPANY DESCRIPTION\n\nEvery institution values excellence. What matters most is why.\nGriffith was created to be a different type of university.  You’ll find we’re\nabout leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of\neducation. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll\nachieve them.\n\nWhy? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe\nand from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and\nchallenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.\n\nPlaying a critical role in supporting Griffith's ambitions is Griffith\nEnterprise [https://www.griffith.edu.au/griffith-enterprise], the university’s\ndedicated commercialisation office, managing and commercialising the\nuniversities intellectual property and research expertise. Griffith Enterprise’s\nmission is to manage and facilitate the commercialisation of intellectual\nproperty and research excellence from Griffith University researchers via the\nmost appropriate commercialisation pathway, ensuring optimum outcomes for all of\nour partners whilst protecting and enhancing the reputation of the university.\nBy translating and commercialising ground-breaking technologies and research\nexcellence, empowering a culture of collaboration, and prioritising our\npartner’s needs we help them achieve their strategic ambitions and generate\nglobal impact.\n\n\nJOB DESCRIPTION\n\nAs the Commercialisation Manager (Biotech) you will be responsible for\nidentifying, developing and leading commercialisation opportunities,\ntransactions and strategic initiatives in the area of life sciences/therapeutics\nas part of the Life Science team that focusses on areas encompassing biomedical\ntechnologies, diagnostics, vaccines, therapeutics and digital health.\n\nYou will work closely with Griffith researchers to identify and assess potential\nnew intellectual property and through business development activities negotiate\ncommercialisation transactions such as licences, start-ups, research agreements\nto take the research to the market.\n\nYou will play a key role in advancing commercialisation awareness and skills\nacross the University and, along with key Griffith staff, engaging with partners\nto help shape strategic partnerships.  As a senior member of the team, you will\nlead all aspects of the commercialisation and IP management process, from\nearly-stage research to the negotiations of deals and establishing start-up\ncompanies.\n\nAbout you\nTo be successful in this role you will hold a postgraduate degree and relevant\nexperience, or 5+ years of experience and a strong track record of success in\nidentifying, managing and commercialising intellectual property in the field of\nLife Science based research through licences, research collaborations and/or\nstart-ups.\n\nYou will also have technical knowledge in a relevant area of Life Sciences and\ndemonstrated business development expertise and a track record will be required.\nYour ability to deal with complex situations and communicate clearly will be an\nasset to the team.\n\nDemonstrated skills required to assess early-stage technologies and understand\nintellectual property (IP) management and protection, including patents and\nother forms of IP; identify and negotiate commercial opportunities; and a proven\nability to scope, pitch and negotiate commercialisation transactions are\nessential.\n\nYou will need to be a self-starter and team player. You will be given the\nautonomy and responsibility to make a significant contribution to Griffith\nEnterprise and the University.\n\nWhat we can offer\nThis is a continuing, full-time position and will be primarily based at Griffith\nUniversity’s Brisbane South (Nathan) or Gold Coast. As Griffith is a multi-site\nUniversity you may be required to work across other locations.  Griffith\nUniversity’s campuses are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera,\nJagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples.\n\nSalary Range\nA competitive remuneration package will be negotiated with the successful\napplicant.\n\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\nWhy Griffith?\nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to\ncreate a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer:\n\n * Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities\n * Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work\n   environment\n * Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts\n * Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading\n * Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff\n   assistance scheme\n\nHow to apply\nAt Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for\nall - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any\naccommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to\nparticipate fully in our recruitment experience.\n\nGriffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage\nAboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply.\nFor more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion\n[https://www.griffith.edu.au/equity#:~:text=At%20Griffith%20we%20understand%20that,safe%2C%20supportive%20and%20productive%20environment]\npage. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against\nall forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s\nModern Slavery Policy\n[https://www.griffith.edu.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0037/1687357/modern-slavery-policy-2022.pdf].\n\nPlease submit your application online and ensure it includes the following:\n\n * A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to\n   the About you section above and the position description\n   [https://c.smartrecruiters.com/sr-company-attachments-prod-aws-dc5/6270a42b9da2f23e08f16ddd/c59f2039-7314-46d6-bf84-f28099266e71?r=s3-eu-central-1])\n * Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details\n * A non-confidential deal sheet highlighting deal track record\n\nApplicants must have unrestricted working rights for the duration of the\nappointment. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position.\n\nSuccessful candidates may be subject to a criminal history check.\n\nFor further information specifically about this role, Dr Mark Ashton, Director,\nGriffith Enterprise on [email protected]\n[/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#ed8a9f848b8b849985888399889f9d9f849e88ad8a9f848b8b9985c3888998c38c98].\n\nFor application support, please contact People Services on +61 (0) 7 373 54011\nquoting reference number REF7588E.\n\nClosing date:  Monday, 26 May 2025 at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be\nsubmitted online.\n\nPlease allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application\nupdate.\n\nReturn only the following JSON structure with extracted values. Do not provide any additional content, explanations, or details:\n\n{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n  \"department\": \"string\", // lowercase format (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n  \"companyName\": \"string\", // UPPERCASE format\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": number,\n    \"max\": number\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"string\", // lowercase format\n    \"string\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": number // in months, if mentioned\n}"}]}]},"modelOutput":{"id":"msg_bdrk_01Ew4R7octYohhTUt6yJneqw","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"typeofEmployment\": \"FULL_TIME\",\n  \"department\": \"research\",\n  \"companyName\": \"GRIFFITH UNIVERSITY\",\n  \"salaryRange\": {\n    \"min\": null,\n    \"max\": null\n  },\n  \"experienceRange\": {\n    \"min\": 5,\n    \"max\": null\n  },\n  \"coreSkills\": [\n    \"intellectual property management\",\n    \"commercialization\",\n    \"business development\",\n    \"research commercialization\",\n    \"patent management\"\n  ],\n  \"technicalSkills\": [\n    \"life sciences\",\n    \"biotech\",\n    \"biomedical technologies\",\n    \"therapeutics\"\n  ],\n  \"softSkills\": [\n    \"communication\",\n    \"negotiation\",\n    \"leadership\",\n    \"self-starter\",\n    \"team player\"\n  ],\n  \"miscellaneousSkills\": [\n    \"deal negotiation\",\n    \"strategic partnership development\",\n    \"research collaboration\"\n  ],\n  \"noticePeriod\": null\n}"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2109,"output_tokens":259}},"recordId":"01JVA02K7A8Q812E329005AGG4"}
{"modelInput":{"anthropic_version":"bedrock-2023-05-31","max_tokens":1024,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Extract the following details from the job description:\n\nEmployment Details:\n- Type of employment (FULL_TIME, PART_TIME, INTERNSHIP, CONTRACT, etc.)\n- Department (e.g., hr, marketing, sales, tech)\n- Company name\n- Salary range (minimum and maximum values)\n- Years of experience required (numeric values for min and max)\n- Notice period requirements (in months)\n\nSkills Requirements:\n- Core skills required for the role\n- Technical skills required (programming languages, software, etc.)\n- Soft skills and interpersonal abilities\n- Miscellaneous skills that don't fit other categories\n\nImportant Instructions:\n- Extract ONLY information explicitly mentioned in the job description\n- Do not infer or fabricate any details not present in the text\n- For type of employment, use UPPERCASE (e.g., FULL_TIME, PART_TIME)\n- For department, use lowercase (e.g., hr, marketing, sales)\n- For company name, use UPPERCASE\n- For all skills, use lowercase format\n- If information for any field is not available, return an empty array or null as appropriate\n- If typeofEmployment or companyName are already present, do not update them\n\nHere is the job description:\n\n<p><strong><span data-contrast=\"none\">Who we are:</span></strong><span\ndata-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134245417&quot;:false,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335551550&quot;:6,&quot;335551620&quot;:6,&quot;335557856&quot;:16777215,&quot;335559739&quot;:220,&quot;335559740&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"none\">Welcome to Archipelago, where we're redefining the\nlandscape of commercial property insurance with our AI-powered data network. We\nbelieve in the power of accurate information to drive meaningful business\ndecisions and offer solutions to generate accurate information as easily and\nefficiently as possible. By connecting brokers, owners, and insurers, we empower\nour customers to navigate the complexities of the property insurance and risk\nmanagement processes with confidence.</span><span\ndata-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134245417&quot;:false,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335551550&quot;:6,&quot;335551620&quot;:6,&quot;335557856&quot;:16777215,&quot;335559739&quot;:220,&quot;335559740&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"none\">Archipelago was founded in 2018 and serves many of\nthe world’s largest property brokers and their clients, representing over 500 of\nthe worlds largest and most dynamic commercial property portfolios to improve\ntheir data and better represent their risks. Archipelago has achieved Series B\nfunding from industry-leading investment partners including Scale, Canaan\nPartners, Ignition Partners, Prologis Ventures, Stone Point Capital, and Zigg\nCapital.</span><span\ndata-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134245417&quot;:false,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335551550&quot;:6,&quot;335551620&quot;:6,&quot;335557856&quot;:16777215,&quot;335559739&quot;:220,&quot;335559740&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"none\">Join us at Archipelago and be part of a team\ndedicated to transforming the commercial property insurance industry. We're\nseeking individuals with a passion for innovation, a commitment to excellence,\nand a drive to further elevate and empower our customers.&nbsp;</span><span\ndata-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134245417&quot;:false,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335551550&quot;:6,&quot;335551620&quot;:6,&quot;335557856&quot;:16777215,&quot;335559739&quot;:220,&quot;335559740&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><span data-contrast=\"none\">If you're ready to make a meaningful impact and be\npart of a dynamic, forward-thinking company, we invite you to explore our job\nopportunities and join us on our journey to keep data accurate and workflows\nseamless.</span><span\ndata-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134245417&quot;:false,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335551550&quot;:6,&quot;335551620&quot;:6,&quot;335557856&quot;:16777215,&quot;335559739&quot;:220,&quot;335559740&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p><strong><em><span data-contrast=\"none\">Note: </span><span\ndata-contrast=\"none\">Preferred candidates to be located in Noida,\nIndia.</span><span\ndata-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134245417&quot;:false,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335551550&quot;:6,&quot;335551620&quot;:6,&quot;335557856&quot;:16777215,&quot;335559739&quot;:220,&quot;335559740&quot;:240}\">\n<span class=\"TextRun MacChromeBold SCXW57828131 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\"\ndata-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW57828131 BCX0\">You will be\nrequired to schedule a portion of your working hours to coincide with our New\nYork-based team, specifically from 9:00 AM to 12:00 PM Eastern Standard\nTime.</span></span><span class=\"EOP SCXW57828131 BCX0\"\ndata-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134245417&quot;:false,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335551550&quot;:6,&quot;335551620&quot;:6,&quot;335557856&quot;:16777215,&quot;335559739&quot;:220,&quot;335559740&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></span></em></strong></p>\n<p data-ccp-border-bottom=\"0px none #000000\" data-ccp-padding-bottom=\"0px\"\ndata-ccp-border-between=\"0px none #000000\"\ndata-ccp-padding-between=\"0px\"><strong><span data-contrast=\"none\">Who you\nare:</span></strong><span\ndata-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134245417&quot;:false,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335551550&quot;:6,&quot;335551620&quot;:6,&quot;335557856&quot;:16777215,&quot;335559739&quot;:220,&quot;335559740&quot;:240,&quot;335572071&quot;:0,&quot;335572072&quot;:0,&quot;335572073&quot;:0,&quot;335572075&quot;:0,&quot;335572076&quot;:0,&quot;335572077&quot;:0,&quot;335572079&quot;:0,&quot;335572080&quot;:0,&quot;335572081&quot;:0,&quot;335572083&quot;:0,&quot;335572084&quot;:0,&quot;335572085&quot;:0,&quot;335572087&quot;:0,&quot;335572088&quot;:0,&quot;335572089&quot;:0,&quot;469789798&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;469789802&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;469789806&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;469789810&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;469789814&quot;:&quot;none&quot;}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p data-ccp-border-bottom=\"0px none #000000\" data-ccp-padding-bottom=\"0px\"\ndata-ccp-border-between=\"0px none #000000\" data-ccp-padding-between=\"0px\"><span\ndata-contrast=\"none\">Archipelago is seeking a Senior Machine Learning Engineer\nto join our growing labs team to work on Gen AI systems. We are looking for an\nengineer who is comfortable with working with full stack development. From\nbuilding models that run in an extraction pipeline to UIs that test and evaluate\nthe results of experiments. We iterate quickly, ship every day, build for the\nlong term, and are looking for smart, independent engineers who want to apply\ntheir trade with like-minded people.</span><span\ndata-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134245417&quot;:false,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335551550&quot;:6,&quot;335551620&quot;:6,&quot;335557856&quot;:16777215,&quot;335559739&quot;:220,&quot;335559740&quot;:240,&quot;335572071&quot;:0,&quot;335572072&quot;:0,&quot;335572073&quot;:0,&quot;335572075&quot;:0,&quot;335572076&quot;:0,&quot;335572077&quot;:0,&quot;335572079&quot;:0,&quot;335572080&quot;:0,&quot;335572081&quot;:0,&quot;335572083&quot;:0,&quot;335572084&quot;:0,&quot;335572085&quot;:0,&quot;335572087&quot;:0,&quot;335572088&quot;:0,&quot;335572089&quot;:0,&quot;469789798&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;469789802&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;469789806&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;469789810&quot;:&quot;none&quot;,&quot;469789814&quot;:&quot;none&quot;}\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p data-ccp-border-between=\"0px none #000000\"\ndata-ccp-padding-between=\"0px\"><strong><span\ndata-contrast=\"none\">Responsibilities</span></strong><span\ndata-contrast=\"none\">:&nbsp;</span><span\ndata-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134245417&quot;:false,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335551550&quot;:6,&quot;335551620&quot;:6,&quot;335557856&quot;:16777215,&quot;335559739&quot;:220,&quot;335559740&quot;:240,&quot;335572071&quot;:0,&quot;33557207